ina, Anil, Ray, Yue), therefore it cannot be in \'not_orderable\' (as it is liked) nor in \'orderable\' (as it is disliked by some).\n\nGiven the constraints, there\'s a strong indication that satisfying all participants might not be possible as for every item there is at least one person who dislikes it and one who likes it. The satisfaction criteria are quite stringent, which leads us to conclude that we cannot fulfill them under the given conditions.\n\nTherefore, our final lists are:\n\n```python\norderable = []\nnot_orderable = []\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 1007, 'num_completion_tokens': 717}
