o more conflicts with her.\n2. Lex is now satisfied (dislikes "ramen") and no more conflicts with him.\n3. Rob is now satisfied (dislikes "ramen") and no more conflicts with him.\n4. Tim is now satisfied (dislikes "ramen") and no more conflicts with him.\n5. Sky is now satisfied (dislikes "ramen") and no more conflicts with her.\n6. Gia is now satisfied (dislikes "ramen") and no more conflicts with her.\n7. Aarav is now satisfied (dislikes "ramen") and no more conflicts with him.\n8. Tom is now satisfied (dislikes "ramen") and no more conflicts with him.\n9. Pat is now satisfied (dislikes "ramen") and no more conflicts with her.\n10. Kai is now satisfied (dislikes "ramen") and no more conflicts with him.\n11. Anil is now satisfied (dislikes "ramen") and no more conflicts with him.\n12. Chao is now satisfied (dislikes "ramen") and no more conflicts with him.\n\nSince "ramen" is settled, let\'s find items that are exclusive likes to some individuals and can be added to \'orderable\':\n\n1. "Waffles" must be \'orderable\' for Liz, Tim, Mina, Shan, and Chen.\n2. "Shawarma" can\'t be \'orderable\' due to conflict with Liz, Lou, Meg, and others.\n3. "Vindaloo" can\'t be \'orderable\' due to conflict with Tom, Jon, Tara, and others.\n4. "Bread" can\'t be \'orderable\' because it conflicts with Xan, Jim, Liz, etc.\n5. "Cake" can\'t be \'orderable\' because it conflicts with Max, Zac, Sid, etc.\n6. "Kimchi" can\'t be \'orderable\' due to conflict with Sue, Kai, and others.\n7. "Hummus" can\'t be \'orderable\' as it\'s disliked by Mina, Ada, and others.\n8. "Peach" can\'t be \'orderable\' due to conflict with Veer, Ron, and others.\n9. "Tart" is disliked by multiple people, so it can\'t be \'orderable\'.\n\nTherefore, the only item that can go in the \'orderable\' list without conflict is:\n\n```python\norderable = [\'waffles\']\n```\n\nNow that we have "waffles" as \'orderable\', we need to go through each individual and ensure there is at least one like on the \'orderable\'