kes salmon, bruschetta; dislikes paneer.\n- Yan likes bruschetta; dislikes kebab, salmon.\n- Lex likes salmon, paneer; dislikes nachos.\n- Dot likes tandoori, salmon, risotto; dislikes none.\n- Ula likes bruschetta; dislikes kebab, paneer.\n- Pia likes korma; dislikes risotto, salmon.\n- Riya likes salmon, bruschetta; dislikes risotto.\n- Vic likes kebab; dislikes paneer, korma.\n- Sol likes risotto; dislikes nachos, paneer.\n- Ray likes risotto, nachos; dislikes salmon.\n- Pat likes korma, tandoori; dislikes paneer.\n\nWe need to place the food items in such a way that likes overlap (to go into 'orderable') and dislikes don't conflict (for 'not_orderable').\n\nFrom the dislikes, we notice that paneer and salmon are the most commonly disliked. However, paneer is liked by many and salmon disliked by some who only like foods that others dislike as well. E.g., Pia only likes korma which is disliked by Vic. This means that salmon cannot go into 'orderable' but can go into 'not_orderable'. \n\nThis will immediately satisfy Tia, Nic, Yan, Sol, Ray, and Riya.\n\nLet's begin by placing items:\n\n- Salmon (disliked by 5: Tia, Yan, Pia, Ray, and Sol; not the sole like for anyone) can go to 'not_orderable'.\n- Paneer can't go in 'not_orderable' because it is liked by Ru who has other likes that are not disliked by anyone (the same reason it also can't go into 'orderable'). We will leave paneer out of both lists for now.\n\nNext, look at other items:\n\n- Nachos are disliked by 3: Tia, Shan, and Lex; but liked by 3: Ru, Chao, Ray.\n- Kebab is disliked by 4: Pam, Shan, Yan, and Ula; liked only by Vic, who dislikes foods that others like. Kebab can go into 'not_orderable'.\n- Risotto is liked by several but only disliked by two: Pia and Riya; it cannot go into 'not_orderable' but can be in 'orderable' due to Pam and Sol who dislike foods that are not liked exclusively by others.\n- Bruschetta is liked by many and not disliked by anyone; it can go into 'orderable'.\n- Tandoori is 