iked by many individuals but not liked by anyone who dislikes it, so it can be placed in 'not_orderable'.\n\nCommon likes that no one disliked (can go in 'orderable'):\n- It seems there are no such items.\n\nItems liked by some and disliked by others (complicated case):\n- Caramel is liked by some and disliked by others, but cannot satisfy all because someone who likes caramel dislikes all other items liked by those who dislike caramel. We cannot include Caramel.\n- Curry is liked by many and only disliked by people who have other likes that can be satisfied, so Curry can be placed in 'orderable'.\n- Fries are liked by many but also disliked by several; however, those who dislike fries have other likes that can be satisfied, so Fries can be placed in 'orderable'.\n- Hummus is liked by some but disliked by others who do have alternative likes, except Mei. We cannot satisfy Mei with the remaining liked items if Hummus is in 'orderable', so Hummus should be in 'not_orderable'. \n- Peach is a bit tricky as it is liked by many but also disliked by many. It cannot go into 'orderable' because Zara dislikes it and has no other likes, also Ray who dislikes Fries would not be satisfied if Peach is 'orderable', so Peach will go in 'not_orderable'.\n- Roti is liked by some but disliked by others, all the individuals who dislike Roti have other items they like except Aarav who also dislikes all other orderable items (Fries and Curry), so Roti cannot go in orderable.\n- Salad is liked by some but disliked by others, all the individuals who dislike Salad have other items they like, so Salad can be placed in 'orderable'.\n- Shrimps are liked by some and disliked by others, Sid and Hu who dislike Shrimps have other likes (Fries), so Shrimps can be placed in 'orderable'.\n\nGiven this analysis, the provisional lists are:\norderable: Curry, Fries, Salad, Shrimps\nnot_orderable: Pizza, Hummus, Peach\n\nLastly, we'll just check if any other liked or disliked food cannot affect the outcomes:\n- Caramel cannot be ordered because it's liked and disliked with no satisfaction overlap.\n- Roti cannot be ordered as Aarav likes only Roti and Hummus which is not orderable.\n\nThese are final lists:\norderable: Curry, Fries, Salad, Shrimps\nnot_orderable: Pizza, Hummus, Peach\n\nNow, we need to verify if everyone's preferences are met. Everyone who dislikes an item in 'not_orderable' or likes an item in 'orderable' must be satisfied.\n\nAfter carefully checking everyone's preferences, it appears that the above list satisfies all individuals' preferences. All individuals either like at least one item on the 'orderable' list or dislike at least one item on the 'not_orderable' list. \n\nThere may be multiple correct solutions due to the complexity of the problem, but as it stands, this solution meets all the given criteria.\n\nSo, the final output will be:\n```python\norderable=['Curry', 'Fries', 'Salad', 'Shrimps'], not_orderable=['Pizza', 'Hummus', 'Peach']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 839, 'num_completion_tokens': 882}
