kes and dislikes of each individual, focusing on identifying any items that must absolutely be in one list or the other based on these preferences. There are a few critical observations that can be made:\n\n1. If any dislike is not liked by anyone else, it should go into the \'not_orderable\' list.\n2. Similarly, if any like is not disliked by anyone, it should go into the \'orderable\' list.\n3. If anyone\'s likes are all disliked by others and vice versa, it\'s an immediate indication that it\'s not possible to satisfy everyone.\n\nStep 1: Check for likes that are not disliked by anyone.\n- Sia likes "peach," but "peach" is disliked by Lei, Jay, Ru, Tim, Jan, Ula, and Kim. Cannot automatically assign "peach".\n- Sia likes "sushi," but "sushi" is disliked by Pat, Ula, and Jaya. Cannot automatically assign "sushi".\n- Sia likes "ravioli," but "ravioli" is disliked by many. Cannot automatically assign "ravioli".\n- Xiu likes "shawarma," but "shawarma" is disliked by Lin and Bao. Cannot automatically assign "shawarma".\n\nThis pattern where each like is also disliked by someone continues for everyone else, so there are no automatic additions to the \'orderable\' list in this step.\n\nStep 2: Check for dislikes that are not liked by anyone.\n- Xiu dislikes "burrito" and "vindaloo," but others like these. Cannot automatically assign to \'not_orderable\'.\n- Lei dislikes "peach," but others like it. Cannot automatically assign "peach".\n- Mia dislikes "ravioli" and "bread," but others like these. Cannot automatically assign to \'not_orderable\'.\n- Riya dislikes "ravioli," but others like it. Cannot automatically assign "ravioli".\n- Jay dislikes "peach" and "burrito," which are liked by others. Cannot automatically assign.\n- Chao dislikes "muffins," but others like it. Cannot automatically assign "muffins".\n- Qi dislikes "muffins" and "ravioli," but others like these. Cannot automatically assign to \'not_orderable\'.\n- Pat dislikes "sushi," but others like it. Cannot automatically assign "sushi".\n- Eli dislikes "bread," but others like it. Cannot automatically assign "bread".\n- Tia dislikes "muffins" and "ravioli," but others like these. Cannot automatically assign to \'not_orderable\'.\n- Lin dislikes "burrito" and "caramel," but others like these. Cannot automatically assign.\n- Eva dislikes "ravioli" and "shawarma," but others like these. Cannot automatically assign to \'not_orderable\'.\n- Ben dislikes "vindaloo," but others like it. Cannot automatically assign "vindaloo".\n- Tim dislikes "bread" and "vindaloo," but these are liked by others. Cannot automatically assign.\n- Bao dislikes "shawarma," but others like it. Cannot automatically assign "shawarma".\n- Aarav dislikes "caramel" and "muffins," but others like these. Cannot automatically assign.\n- Isha dislikes "vindaloo" and "caramel," which are liked by others. Cannot automatically assign.\n- Jaya dislikes "sushi," but others like it. Cannot automatically assign "sushi".\n- Jan dislikes "peach" and "bread," but these are liked by others. Cannot automatically assign.\n- Kim dislikes "muffins" and "ravioli," which are liked by others. Cannot automatically assign.\n- Fay dislikes "caramel," but others like it. Cannot automatically assign "caramel".\n- Rex dislikes "muffins," which are liked by others. Cannot automatically assign "muffins".\n- Ula dislikes "burrito" and "peach," which are liked by others. Cannot automatically assign.\n\nSince there were no likes that weren\'t also a dislike and no dislikes that weren\'t also liked by someone else, we can not automatically add anything to either list based on Step 1 and Step 2.\n\nNow, I will try to identify items that must be added to one list or the other based on constraints that will satisfy the most people.\n\n- Since "ravioli" is liked by several but also disliked by several, and satisfying those who dislike it seems to have a greater impact, we should put "ravioli" in the \'not_orderable\' list.\nRecapping:\n   