e but not disliked by anyone (must be in 'orderable'):\n1. cake - Liked by Ru, Jun, Shan, Leo and not disliked by anyone.\n2. curry - Liked by Meg, Ula and not disliked by anyone (Min dislikes curry, so it can't be on the orderable list).\n3. shrimps - Liked by Max, Riya, Diya, Ying and not disliked by anyone (Fay dislikes shrimps, so it can't be on the orderable list).\n\nItems disliked by some but not liked by anyone (must be in 'not_orderable'):\n1. brownies - Disliked by Ian, Lin, Ansh, Bao, Tia, Gus, Qi, Ana (Min and Isha like brownies, so it can't be on the not_orderable list).\n\nNow let's start with the orderable list:\n\n1. cake - It must be on the orderable list.\n\nNext, let's see which items have conflict:\n\n- salmon - Liked by many but disliked by Fay and Wei.\n- bread - Liked by many but disliked by Isha, Bao, Shan, Vic, Ula, Ana.\n- poke - Liked by many but disliked by more.\n- brownies, curry, peach, burrito, pie - Liked and disliked by some.\n\nWe must now try to satisfy everyone by placing at least one liked item on the orderable list or one disliked item on the not_orderable list.\n\nIt seems problematic to satisfy both Fay (dislikes salmon) and the many people who like salmon, such as Ian, Max, Ron, Ana, Zoe, Xan. Since there's only one person who dislikes cake and it's Leo, it looks like we would need to satisfy Leo with another of his dislikes, which are brownies and curry.\n\nConsidering that:\n\nLeo dislkes both brownies and curry, which are liked by many, so we cannot have brownies or curry on 'not_orderable' to satisfy Leo.\nMeg dislikes poke and burrito, and since poke is a conflicted item with many disliking it, if we can satisfy Meg with curry and not have poke on orderable (satisfying the ones who dislike poke), we are on the right track.\nAna dislikes both brownies and bread, which may push bread to the 'not_orderable' list since there's less conflict with that compared to brownies.\n\nGiven these observations, let's put poke and brea