ecake, if cheesecake is 'orderable' then Mina is satisfied.\n- Hal likes cheesecake, if cheesecake is 'orderable' then Hal is satisfied.\n- The others either have their likes or dislikes already met by the current lists or have multiple likes where at least one can accommodate them (like Rex who likes caramel and cheesecake, with cheesecake 'orderable').\n\nAfter considering all preferences, the final solution would be to have 'udon' and 'cheesecake' as 'orderable', and 'caramel' and 'peach' as 'not_orderable'. This final list will satisfy everyone in the group without any conflicts.\n\nWe cannot include soup in either list to prevent conflicts. At least one liked item of every individual is in the 'orderable' list or one disliked item is in the 'not_orderable' list.\n\nSo the final lists are:\n```python\norderable=['udon', 'cheesecake'], not_orderable=['caramel', 'peach']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 555, 'num_completion_tokens': 1310}
