dy satisfied with "Cake". Mei, Pam, Sue, and Kavi, despite liking "Sushi", were satisfied by either disliking "Cake" or "Hummus", now on the \'orderable\' list. Sid dislikes both "Cake" and "Hummus", therefore "Sushi" should also go on the \'orderable\' list.\n\nWe are left with a couple of like/dislikes to consider that haven\'t been satisfied by existing items on either list: \n- Zoe dislikes "Sushi", "Mousse", and "Cake".\n- Max dislikes "Hummus", "Mousse", and "Sushi".\n\nSince Zoe and Max have demands in conflict with the current orderable items, it is impossible to satisfy all participants with a combination of these four items. Hence, we would have to return empty lists, as there is no combination that can satisfy all participants:\n\n```python\norderable = []\nnot_orderable = []\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 743, 'num_completion_tokens': 1214}
