ic, Mel, Ansh, Sky, Om, Pam, Kim, Joe, Ned, Abe, Sia, Diya, Lou, and others; Liked by various individuals like Cal, Joy, Ava, Max, Shan, Riya, Ben, Rohan, Ping, etc.\n\n- **Ravioli**: Disliked by Jim, Cal, Zoe, Vic, Xia, Shan, Max, Taj, Aarav, Chao, Naina, Cy, Xiu, and many others; Liked by a number of people like Ron, Shan, Xan, Ian, Jan, Aarav, Du, Abe, Pat, Kit, etc.\n\n- **Sorbet**: Disliked by Fay, Jim, Bao, Ben, Mel, Lex, Sia, Chao, Xiu, Naina, and others; Liked by Jaya, Oli, Riya, Jay, Lex, Raj, Rob, Xiu, Cy etc.\n\n### Universally or predominately liked:\n- **Couscous**: Liked by Fay, Lee, Cal, Tom, Sue, Meg, and others; Disliked by Ron, Wes, Yan, Kim, Ben, Kai, Nic, Du, Li, Rob, Naina, etc. which makes it contentious.\n\n- **Espresso**: Liked by Yue, Eva, Kim, Kai, Liv, Dot, Kim, Du, Sue, Pam, and others; Disliked by Sol, Sky, May, Rohan, Lex, Chen, Raj, Lei, and a few more, making it also contentious.\n\n- **Wonton**: Liked by Yue, Eva, Amy, Tim, Abe, Sam, Sol, Ned, Min, Raj, Anil, etc.; Disliked by Ray, Jaya, May, Aarav, Taj, Chen, Chao, Meg, Pam, and others, also making it a divisive choice.\n\nTo attempt to create an orderable/not_orderable list that satisfies everyone, we must look for items that can satisfy the maximum number of individuals without conflict. \n\nTo maximize the satisfaction and minimize conflicts, we could start by selecting items that are liked by people who have unique dislikes, as placing their liked item in "orderable" would resolve their satisfaction without forcing an item in "not_orderable".\n\nConsidering no item is overwhelmingly liked or disliked, the task is complex. Let\'s look at making sure disliked items are not universally liked by someone else.\n\n1. **Risotto** is a good candidate for the "not_orderable" list, as it\'s disliked by many, but we should confirm no one only likes risotto without liking anything else.\n2. **Sorbet** can be considered for "not_orderable" given the number of people disliking it, provided it