 sushi, cake. Leo: Likes falafel, shawarma. Dislikes custard. Ian: Likes cake, custard. Dislikes sushi. Ru: Likes cheese, roti. Dislikes pancakes. Lee: Likes roti. Dislikes sushi, falafel. Bea: Likes custard, roti, sushi. Lei: Dislikes shawarma, cake, roti. Du: Likes cheese. Dislikes pancakes, falafel. Jun: Likes cheese. Dislikes pancakes, roti. Jaya: Likes roti, sushi, cheese. Tom: Dislikes cake, pancakes, falafel. Lin: Likes falafel. Dislikes shawarma, cheese. Amy: Dislikes roti, custard, shawarma. Lex: Likes roti. Dislikes pancakes, custard. Fay: Likes cake, custard. Dislikes roti. Ada: Likes pancakes. Dislikes cheese, roti. Sam: Likes roti, pancakes. Dislikes sushi. Joy: Likes cheese, custard. Dislikes sushi. Tao: Likes cake, cheese, pancakes. Tara: Likes cake. Dislikes shawarma, custard. Vic: Likes custard, sushi. Dislikes roti. Rina: Likes falafel, roti. Dislikes pancakes. Ying: Likes cheese, roti. Dislikes sushi. Val: Likes falafel. Dislikes sushi, custard. Ping: Likes pancakes, shawarma, falafel. Kavi: Likes roti, pancakes, falafel. Yan: Likes shawarma. Dislikes roti, custard. Diya: Likes custard, cake. Dislikes roti. Ivy: Likes custard. Dislikes falafel, shawarma. Joe: Likes shawarma, pancakes, custard. Sky: Likes sushi. Dislikes cheese, falafel. Cy: Likes cheese, custard. Dislikes roti. Pam: Likes cake, custard, pancakes. Geet: Likes custard. Dislikes cake, pancakes. Tia: Likes cake. Dislikes cheese, sushi. Eli: Dislikes custard, sushi, pancakes. Hu: Likes custard. Dislikes shawarma, sushi. Jan: Likes pancakes, roti. Dislikes cake. Om: Likes falafel. Dislikes cake, roti. Wes: Dislikes custard, falafel, sushi. Veer: Likes cheese. Dislikes sushi, falafel. Xiu: Likes sushi, cheese. Dislikes custard. Cal: Likes cake, shawarma. Dislikes falafel. Ben: Likes roti. Dislikes custard, cheese. Zara: Likes cake. Dislikes sushi, falafel. Wei: Dislikes roti, cheese, sushi. Ansh: Likes cake. Dislikes pancakes, falafel. Ula: Likes falafel. Dislikes shawarma, cake. Raj: Dislikes cheese, custard, shawarma. Max: Likes shawarma. Dislikes custard, falafel. Pat: Likes roti. Dislikes sushi, cheese. Hal: Likes cheese, custard. Dislikes shawarma. Oli: Likes shawarma, roti, custard. Zan: Likes cheese, shawarma. Dislikes sushi. Kit: Likes shawarma, cake. Dislikes roti. Liv: Likes shawarma. Dislikes roti, cheese. Ned: Likes sushi. Dislikes cake, cheese. Gen: Likes cheese. Dislikes shawarma, custard. Mel: Likes custard. Dislikes pancakes, cake. ', 'menu_items': ['shawarma', 'falafel', 'sushi', 'cake', 'cheese', 'pancakes', 'roti', 'custard'], 'gpt_out': 'Let\'s approach this by first listing the items liked and disliked by the individuals to get a sense of common preferences. To satisfy everyone, all liked items of one person cannot be in the \'not_orderable\' list, and all disliked items cannot be in the \'orderable\' list.\n\nWe can start by putting universally disliked items into the \'not_orderable\' list and universally liked items into the \'orderable\' list. Then we\'ll have to find a compromise for other items.\n\nLooking at the likes and dislikes, we see:\n- "Sushi" is liked by many and is the only liked item by some (Bao, Sky, Ned), so it cannot be placed into the \'not_orderable\' list, but it is also disliked by some (Ava, Isha, Lia, Lee, Ying, Wes, Veer, Xiu, Wei, Pat, Zan, Raj).\n- "Shawarma" is liked by many but also disliked by many (Mina, Mei, Isha, Lei, Tara, Yan, Ivy, Hu, Raj, Ula, Zara, Gen, Liv), so it will be challenging to place.\n- "Pancakes" is liked by many people. However, it is a disliked item for some (Taj, Ava, Nic, Isha, Kai, Du, Jun, Rina, Eli, Ansh, Mel), meaning we cannot put this in \'orderable\' if any of these individuals have no other liked items on the list or if it is their only disliked item.\n- "Roti" appears to be more frequently disliked. We may consider it for the \'not_orderable\' list.\n- "Cake" is also divisive, liked by some and disliked by others (Eva, Arun, Lei, Tia, Geet, Pam, Wes, Ula, Ansh, Zara).\n- "Falafel" has supporters and opposers, hence complicated to be placed into either list.\n- "Custard" is liked by many, and could probably be placed into the \'orderable\' list since only a few dislike it (Bea, Tara, Eli, Raj, Wes).\n- "Cheese" is liked by many but is disliked by some (Eva, Liz, Lou, Xan, Tom, Rina, Ying, Jun, Lei, Tia, Tara, Vic, Jan, Liv, Zara, Raj, Wei, Pat, Gen).\n\nLet\'s try placing "roti" in the \'not_orderable\' list and "custard" in the \'orderable\' list to start with and see if this satisfies everyone:\n\n- "Roti" dislikes: Eva, Liz, Dot, Amy, Jun, Lei, Ivan, Sam, Ying, Wei, Lee, Xin, Lex, Cal, Om, Ansh, Raj, Gen, Pam, Pat, Ben.\n- "Custard" dislikes: Bea, Tara, Eli, Wes, Raj.\n\nPlacing "roti" in \'not_orderable\' satisfies Eva, Liz, Dot, Amy, Jun, Lei, Ivan, Sam, Ying, Wei, Lee, Xin, Lex, Cal, Om, Ansh, Raj, Gen, Pam, Pat, and Ben.\n\nPlacing "custard" in \'orderable\' would displease Bea, Tara, Eli, Wes but satisfies Taj, Dot, Arun, Riya, Lia, Geet, Hu, Ian, Diya, Ivy, Joe, Joy, Cy, Hal, Mel, which is a larger number.\n\nNone of the participants have both "roti" and "custard" as only disliked items, so having "roti" as \'not_orderable\' and "custard" as \'orderable\' doesn\'t disqualify anyone outright. However, we must ensure that those who dislike "custard" or "roti" must have other items they like on the \'orderable\' list or other disliked items on the \'not_orderable\' list.\n\nNow we need to select additional items very carefully, making sure that for each individual who dislikes "custard", there\'s at least one item they like that\'s \'orderable\' or one other item they dislike that\'s \'not_orderable\'.\n\nLet\'s examine the case for each person:\n\n1. Bea: Likes sushi, needs sushi to be in \'orderable\'.\n2. Tara: Likes cake, needs cake in \'orderable\'.\n3. Eli: Dislikes pancakes, sushi, and custard. If we place pancakes in \'not_orderable\', Eli will be satisfied.\n4. Wes: Dislikes custard, sushi, and falafel. One of sushi or falafel must be in \'not_orderable\' to satisfy Wes.\n\nSince Eli and Wes need different items in \'not_orderable\', we face a conflict that makes it impossible to satisfy both Eli and Wes simultaneously if we were to include their exclusively disliked items. However, satisfying Eli\'s conditions seems to be more straightforward since pancakes are disliked by more individuals than falafel.\n\nWe can place "pancakes" in the \'not_orderable\' to satisfy Eli, but for Wes, we\'d then have to ensure he has a liked item in the \'orderable\' or another disliked in the \'not_orderable\'. But Wes dislikes all three items we\'re considering placing in lists, leaving no option that satisfies all criteria.\n\nTherefore, based on the conflicts and the complex intersections of likes and dislikes, it appears that no combination of \'orderable\' and \'not_orderable\' lists would satisfy every individual in this scenario. Hence, the solution is:\n\n```python\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 1233, 'num_completion_tokens': 1166}
