obster being available:\n\n- Ava: Likes lobster, satisfied.\n- Pam: Does not like lobster or curry, not satisfied.\n- Riya: Likes lobster, satisfied.\n- Sue: Does not like curry or lobster, not satisfied.\n- Nic: Likes curry, satisfied.\n- Ana: Likes curry and lobster, satisfied.\n- Bao: Likes lobster, satisfied.\n- Shan: Likes curry, satisfied.\n\nWe have a problem that Pam and Sue are not satisfied since they only like Ratatouille and/or Omelette. Let's try to include Omelette on the 'orderable' list to satisfy them.\n\n'Orderable': Curry, Lobster, Omelette\n\n'Not_orderable': Ratatouille\n\nNow, all participants who like Ratatouille are satisfied with either Curry or Lobster. So are all participants who like Omelette. We will once again check satisfaction:\n\n- Pam: Likes Omelette, now satisfied.\n- Sue: Likes Omelette, now satisfied.\n\nEveryone is now potentially satisfied, but we need to make sure that including Omelette doesn't dissatisfy anyone who dislikes it since Omelette has some dislikes associated with it:\n\n- Joe dislikes Omelette but is satisfied with Curry.\n- Ray dislikes Omelette but is satisfied with Tart.\n- Jaya dislikes Omelette but dislikes everything so can't be satisfied (which is not a blocking condition, as their satisfaction is impossible by default).\n- Feng dislikes Lobster but is satisfied with Curry and Omelette.\n- Li dislikes Lobster and Curry but is satisfied by Omelette.\n- Tia dislikes Omelette but is satisfied by Lobster.\n- Tim dislikes Omelette but is satisfied by Curry.\n- Nic dislikes Omelette but is satisfied by Curry.\n- Ping dislikes Tart and is satisfied with Curry and Omelette.\n- Hal dislikes Omelette but dislikes everything so can't be satisfied (which is not a blocking condition, as their satisfaction is impossible by default).\n- May dislikes Omelette but dislikes everything so can't be satisfied (which is not a blocking condition, as their satisfaction is impossible by default).\n- Sid dislikes Omelette but is satisfied by Tart.\n\nIncluding Omelette doesn’t dissatisfy those who dislike it because they are all satisfied by either Curry, Lobster, or Tart. However, even with Omelette, Jaya, Hal, and May remain unsatisfied due to their overall dislikes outweighing their likes.\n\nSo our final solution considering the above is:\n\n```\norderable = ['curry', 'lobster', 'omelette']\nnot_orderable = ['ratatouille']\n```\n\nLet's format this as requested:\n\n```python\norderable=['curry', 'lobster', 'omelette'], not_orderable=['ratatouille']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 609, 'num_completion_tokens': 1101}
