ed. This leads us to a dead end, since we can't exclusively place tacos in either 'orderable' or 'not_orderable' without displeasing someone.\n\nFrom the given constraints and analysis:\n\n- Bread must be 'orderable' to satisfy those who like it and because those who dislike it have other items they can like.\n- Cheesecake, risotto, and tacos cannot be placed definitively in either 'orderable' or 'not_orderable' because of exclusive likes/dislikes that would leave someone unsatisfied.\n\nHence, there's no possible way to meet the criteria for all participants.\n\nOutput should be:\n```python\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 736, 'num_completion_tokens': 936}
