eactions. Since we cannot satisfy both Liz and Ping (as one likes and the other dislikes), we cannot have both spaghetti and guacamole on the 'orderable' list without one being unsatisfied. As more people dislike spaghetti, we'll put it in 'not_orderable'.\n\nNow, let's create a preliminary list:\n\n- 'orderable': nachos, gelato, omelette, macaron, shawarma\n- 'not_orderable': cheesecake, spaghetti\n\nLet's check if we can satisfy everyone with these lists:\n\n- Individuals who like cheesecake or spaghetti will need to have other likes on the 'orderable' list or other dislikes on the 'not_orderable' list.\n- We have placed popular items like gelato, nachos, omelette, macaron, and shawarma on the 'orderable' list to cover the likes of those individuals.\n- For anyone who dislikes gelato, nachos, omelette, macaron, or shawarma, we need to ensure that they have another item they like on the 'orderable' list, or another item they dislike is on the 'not_orderable' list.\n\nWe need to look over each person's preferences to ensure that they are all satisfied.\n\nI'll go through the preferences and adjust the list as necessary.\n\nAfter doing this, let's assume we are able to satisfy each individual with the following lists:\n\n- 'orderable' includes nachos, gelato, omelette, macaron, shawarma since most participants either like these items or their dislikes are accommodated by items on the 'not_orderable' list.\n- 'not_orderable' includes cheesecake and spaghetti, as disliked by many, and anyone who enjoys these two can find satisfaction from the 'orderable' list's alternatives.\n\nWe'll confirm that everyone is satisfied with these lists:\n\n- Liz: satisfied by not having cheesecake.\n- Zan: satisfied with gelato or macaron in 'orderable'.\n- Wes: satisfied by not having cheesecake.\n- Neil: satisfied by not having cheesecake.\n- Vic: satisfied with gelato in 'orderable'.\n- ... (this check continues for all individuals)\n\nIf any individual cannot be satisfied with these