s (7 dislikes)\n- Pizza: Disliked by Chao, Ivy, Lei, and Val (4 dislikes)\n- Sushi: Disliked by Diya, Liz, Geet, and Du (4 dislikes)\n- Kimchi: Disliked by Chao, Nita, Amy, Tim, Du, and Zan (6 dislikes)\n- Bruschetta: Disliked by Diya, Liv, and Zan (3 dislikes)\n\nCommon Likes:\n- Vegetables: Liked by Chao, Diya, Joy, and Tim (4 likes)\n- Ramen: Liked by Liz and Ben (2 likes)\n- Waffles: Liked by Joy, Liv, and Zan (3 likes)\n- Bruschetta: Liked by Lei, Wes, and Zara (3 likes)\n\nStep 1: Place "peach" on the not_orderable list, since it is disliked by the majority and only liked by 3. \n\nNot_orderable: ["peach"]\n\nStep 2: Check if any of the people who like peach are dissatisfied with peach being not orderable:\n\n- Lei also likes bruschetta.\n- Tim also likes vegetables.\n- Zara also likes bruschetta.\n\nSince they have other likes that haven\'t been dismissed yet, they can still be satisfied without peach being orderable.\n\nStep 3: Place "kimchi" on the not_orderable list, as it has quite a few dislikes.\n\nNot_orderable: ["peach", "kimchi"]\n\nStep 4: Check if any of the people who like kimchi are dissatisfied with kimchi being not orderable:\n\n- Geet also likes pizza (which hasn\'t been addressed yet).\n- Ron also likes pizza.\n- Du only likes pizza aside from kimchi.\n\nSince Geet and Ron have another like (pizza) and we haven\'t placed pizza on the not_orderable list yet, they could potentially be satisfied. Du can have his satisfaction through pizza as well.\n\nStep 5: We now look for items to add to the orderable list. Our best candidates are those liked by many but not disliked too much.\n\n- Bruschetta is liked by a few and is not a common dislike, so we add it to the orderable list.\n\nOrderable: ["bruschetta"]\n\nStep 6: Validate that everyone who dislikes bruschetta still has satisfaction conditions:\n\n- Diya likes vegetables and sushi (not addressed yet).\n- Liv likes waffles (not addressed yet).\n- Zan likes waffles (not addressed yet).\n\nSince t