ked item on the `orderable` list or one disliked item on the `not_orderable` list, without conflict.\n\nLet\'s analyze the dislikes to find items for `not_orderable`:\n\n- Quiche is disliked by Sol and Amy, but liked by Eli, Yue, and Ravi, so it cannot be in `not_orderable`.\n- Shrimps are disliked by Sam, Sal, Ping, Yan, and Eva, but liked by Sol, Anil, Xan, Chen and Eva, so it cannot be in `not_orderable`.\n- Salad is disliked by Sam, Mel, Anil, Xiu, Mina, Rex, but liked by Xan and Rex, so it cannot be in `not_orderable`.\n- Paneer is disliked by Sam, Xan and Ula, but liked by Amy, Eli, Mel, Anil, Hal, Bo, and Ravi, so it cannot be in `not_orderable`.\n- Custard is disliked by Eli, Sal, Mina and Yan, but liked by Xiu, Bo, Chen, and Eva, so it cannot be in `not_orderable`.\n- Gelato is disliked by Sal and Mel, but liked by Yue, so it cannot be in `not_orderable`.\n- Pie is disliked by Xiu, Mina, and Rex, but no one has it as a liked item, so it can be in `not_orderable`.\n- Risotto is disliked by Ping, but liked by Amy, Ula, and Eva, so it cannot be in `not_orderable`.\n- Caramel is disliked by Hal, but liked by Yan, so it cannot be in `not_orderable`.\n\nBased on the above analysis, only "pie" can be added to `not_orderable`.\n\nNow let\'s find items for the `orderable` list. We need to find liked items that are not disliked by anyone else:\n\n- Muffins are liked by Sol, Yue, Ula, and Ping but are disliked by Chen, so it cannot be in `orderable`.\n- Quiche, as determined above, cannot be included in `not_orderable` and is liked by several, so it must be in `orderable`.\n- Risotto is liked by Amy, Ula, and Eva but disliked by Ping, so it cannot be in `orderable`.\n- Paneer is liked by many but disliked by several people, so it cannot be in `orderable`.\n- Custard and caramel are both liked and disliked, so they can\'t be in `orderable`.\n- Shrimps, salad, and gelato are liked by some but disliked by others, so they cannot be in `orderable`.\n\nAfter analyzing the p