e there is a potential to satisfy dependencies for those who dislike \'Korma\', adding \'Korma\' to \'orderable\' seems like a feasible option:\n\n`orderable = [\'Korma\']`\n\nNow we continue to identify another item to add to \'orderable\'. \'Quiche\' looks promising as several individuals still not satisfied with \'Korma\' like \'Quiche\', and it hasn\'t been universally disliked:\n\n- Ned likes \'Quiche\' and is already satisfied as \'Korma\' is not in his dislikes.\n- Hal likes \'Quiche\'.\n\nAdding \'Quiche\' to \'orderable\' satisfies Hal and is fine for others, but we have Sue, Shan, Ying, Eli, and Pia who will be dissatisfied if \'Quiche\' is not on \'orderable\'. Looking at their preferences:\n\n- Sue likes \'Churros\' and dislikes \'Sorbet\'. \'Churros\' can potentially be \'orderable\'.\n- Shan dislikes \'Korma\', so she\'s already satisfied, and she likes \'Quiche\'.\n- Ying likes \'Shrimps\'. We\'ll have to check the feasibility of adding \'Shrimps\' to \'orderable\'.\n- Eli likes \'Salad\', which is highly contested and thus is risky to add to \'orderable\'.\n- Pia likes \'Sorbet\', which we can\'t add to \'orderable\' because it\'s widely disliked.\n\nThus, adding \'Quiche\' seems less feasible considering the satisfaction of others. We should look for another item:\n\n- \'Churros\' is liked by many who have not been satisfied yet, and it is plausible to add since not many have it on their dislike list who aren\'t already satisfied by \'Korma\'.\n\nLet\'s try adding \'Churros\' to \'orderable\':\n\n`orderable = [\'Korma\', \'Churros\']`\n\nThis satisfies Gen, Sue, Lan, Chen, Geet, Dan, Diya, and others who like it.\n\nNow we continue with this method, looking for other liked items that will bring overall satisfaction without causing dissatisfaction for anybody else. We will need the \'not_orderable\' list to contain items only disliked and not liked by anyone. We can add \'Sorbet\' to it as it\'s disliked by many but necessary for some to be satisfied