erson dislikes an item, it must be in the `not_orderable` list.\n2. No item can appear on both the `orderable` and the `not_orderable` lists.\n3. Every person must be satisfied with the combination of the two lists.\n\nLet's start by identifying items that can be straightforwardly classified as `orderable` or `not_orderable` by considering dislikes only, because dislikes immediately qualify items to be in the `not_orderable` list if no one has the item on their like list. \n\n**Step 1: Find unanimously disliked items for `not_orderable` list.**\n\n- `pie` - only Ravi, Ian, Tao, Tim, Shan, Pat, Ansh, Sid, and Xan like pie, and many dislike it, so it cannot be immediately placed in the `not_orderable` list.\n- `lasagna` - Although disliked by many, it is liked by a few, so it can't go into `not_orderable` either.\n- `ramen` - liked by some, cannot go into `not_orderable`.\n- `kebab` - liked by many, cannot go into `not_orderable`.\n- `salmon` - liked by some, cannot go into `not_orderable`.\n- `ravioli` - liked by some, cannot go into `not_orderable`.\n- `paneer` - liked by some, cannot go into `not_orderable`.\n- `shawarma` - liked by some, cannot go into `not_orderable`.\n- `frittata` - liked by some, cannot go into `not_orderable`.\n\nThere are no items that are unanimously disliked. Therefore, we must think about likes and try to maximize the number of people satisfied by considering trade-offs.\n\n**Step 2: Find inevitable `orderable` items by looking for a unique liked item.**\n\nIf a person has a unique liked item that no one dislikes, this item must go into the `orderable` list. By going through each person's preferences:\n\n- Gus, Eva, Bao, Pam, Cy, Om, Qi, Naina, Jun, Mei, and Chen dislike `paneer` but this does not make it a candidate for `not_orderable` since there are several individuals who like it (Gen, Yue, Tia, Lex, Anil, Eli, Liv, Leo, Wei, Sol, Ula, Sky, Cal, Ty, Xiu, and Xin).\n- Also, the likes of `lasagna`, `ravioli`, `kebab`, `salmon`, `ramen`, 