les. Lin: Likes brownies. Dislikes waffles, bruschetta. Lou: Likes bruschetta, korma. Dislikes espresso. Ray: Likes espresso, cake. Dislikes waffles. Jay: Likes bruschetta. Dislikes cake, waffles. Lei: Likes korma, cake, brownies. Sue: Likes cake. Dislikes brownies, espresso. Ned: Dislikes toast, espresso, cake. Isha: Likes brownies, korma. Dislikes toast. Val: Likes korma. Dislikes espresso, cake. Raj: Likes waffles. Dislikes brownies, cake. Fay: Likes cake, toast. Dislikes waffles. Tara: Likes korma. Dislikes cake, brownies. Arun: Likes bruschetta, cake. Dislikes toast. Amy: Likes toast, korma, waffles. Oli: Likes brownies. Dislikes espresso, waffles. Veer: Likes brownies. Dislikes bruschetta, waffles. Ping: Likes korma. Dislikes brownies, waffles. Nita: Likes brownies. Dislikes waffles, bruschetta. Pam: Likes bruschetta. Dislikes espresso, cake. Jim: Likes waffles. Dislikes bruschetta, espresso. Ivy: Likes espresso, waffles. Dislikes korma. Joe: Likes waffles, korma. Dislikes bruschetta. Chen: Likes waffles, korma. Dislikes toast. Ian: Likes espresso, korma. Dislikes toast. Rob: Likes korma, bruschetta. Dislikes waffles. Pia: Likes korma. Dislikes cake, waffles. Rohan: Likes waffles, cake. Dislikes espresso. Eva: Dislikes espresso, brownies, cake. Cy: Likes brownies. Dislikes espresso, toast. ', 'menu_items': ['korma', 'bruschetta', 'brownies', 'espresso', 'waffles', 'toast', 'cake'], 'gpt_out': "To solve this, we need to find a combination of orderable and not_orderable items that satisfy everyone's likes and dislikes according to the given criteria. Let's analyze the likes and dislikes to figure out a possible combination.\n\nFirst, let's identify the items that are unanimously disliked, as these items can never be included in the 'orderable' list:\n\n- Espresso is disliked by Ana, Anil, Bo, Eva, Jan, Jaya, Lou, Ned, Oli, Pam, Rob, Sia, Val, Wei, and several others.\n- Brownies are disliked by Ana, Isha, Mina, Naina, Shan, Tara and Eva.\n- Waffles are disliked 