issatisfy the ones who like it because they can potentially be satisfied by other items.\n- To ensure we don't exclude any item that is the only liked item of one individual, we check if any person's sole liked item ends up on 'not_orderable'. Nic likes fries and dislikes toast and custard, so we have to be careful not to put all of Nic's disliked items on 'not_orderable' and exclude fries from 'orderable'. However, fries can be 'not_orderable' still, as long as we include the loves of those who like fries in 'orderable' to ensure satisfaction.\n- As soup is liked by many and the dislikes don't create overwhelming conflicts, it could be put on 'orderable'.\n- Similarly, nachos can be on 'orderable' since the likes outweigh the dislikes and there's not a significant conflict.\n\nStep 3: Finalizing choices\n- Fries will be 'not_orderable'.\n- Soup and nachos will be 'orderable'.\n- We need one more 'orderable' item to ensure that Ron, who dislikes fries and waffles, is satisfied. Hummus can be his satisfying item as only Jan and Zara dislike it, and they have other likes that can be included in 'orderable'.\n- We must include doughnut in 'orderable' to keep Abe satisfied, as doughnut and nachos are the only likeable items for Abe, and nachos are already in 'orderable'.\n- Waffles and toast must be avoided in 'not_orderable' due to Ray liking fries and not having any other options if fries are in 'not_orderable'.\n\nThe orderable list will then be: nachos, soup, hummus, doughnut.\nThe not_orderable list will be: fries.\n\nNow let's ensure that all individuals can be satisfied under these lists:\n\n- Tim likes nachos, which is orderable.\n- Aarav dislikes soup, but likes nachos, which is orderable.\n- Ron dislikes fries, which is not_orderable, and likes hummus, which is orderable.\n- Jan likes doughnuts, which is orderable.\n- Liv likes both custard and soup; soup is orderable.\n- Pia likes custard, but since soup is orderable and fries are not_orderable, there's satisfaction.\n- Nic dislikes fries and one other item is orderable (we ensured that at least one of the likes is orderable to satisfy).\n- Abe likes doughnut, which is orderable.\n- Dan dislikes fries, which is not_orderable, and likes shawarma, which isn’t a conflict here.\n- Cal dislikes fries, shawarma, and custard, but as none of his dislikes are orderable, he's neutral and hence satisfied.\n- Ned dislikes toast, waffles, shawarma, none of which are orderable, so satisfaction is incurred.\n- Ping likes toast and hummus; hummus is orderable.\n- Nita dislikes doughnut and toast; both are not_orderable so she's satisfied.\n- Zara likes toast and dislikes hummus and custard; toast being liked is not on not_orderable.\n- Kai dislikes fries and likes hummus; fries are not_orderable and hummus is orderable.\n- Zan likes shawarma and dislikes fries; fries being not_orderable is good.\n- Diya dislikes hummus, custard, and likes nachos; nachos are orderable.\n- Ravi likes custard, shawarma, and dislikes doughnut; but doughnut is orderable fulfilling satisfaction criteria.\n- Du dislikes waffles and likes nachos which are orderable.\n- Pat dislikes nachos and shawarma but likes doughnut, which is orderable.\n- Ben dislikes fries, which are not_orderable, and likes other items, one of which is orderable.\n- Ray likes fries but dislikes waffles, doughnut, and since fries are not_orderable, he is satisfied.\n- Hui likes toast, not part of not_orderable, dislikes fries, which is not_orderable.\n- Feng dislikes custard, likes fries and soup; soup is orderable.\n- Chen likes waffles, soup, doughnut; waffles are not on not_orderable, and soup and doughnut are orderable.\n- Rohan dislikes custard and likes doughnut and toast; doughnut is orderable.\n- Ru likes toast, hummus and dislikes shawarma; hummus is orderable.\n- Oli dislikes hummus, likes soup and waffles; soup is orderable.\n- Cy dislikes nothing, likes items including those that are orderable.\n- Mei likes soup and waffles, 