le dislikes, which makes it challenging to place them confidently in either list without further analysis.\n\nLet's attempt to satisfy individuals with conflicting preferences:\n\nSince Risotto and Sorbet can be in the 'not_orderable' list:\n\nKen, Val, Raj, Fay, Sam, Xan, Eva, Ru, and Nita are satisfied with Espresso being 'orderable'.\nMax, Om, Ru, and Wes dislike Risotto, which is 'not_orderable', so they are satisfied.\n\nSince we cannot satisfy everyone due to the conflicting preferences, we cannot form valid 'orderable' and 'not_orderable' lists. Thus, the output will be:\n\n```python\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 848, 'num_completion_tokens': 791}
