e\' list if that means someone who likes it would be unsatisfied due to nothing they like being \'orderable\'.\n\nFurther observation shows that "tart" is liked by many people. If we put "tart" in the \'not_orderable\' list, it would be very difficult to satisfy all those who like "tart". Thus, "tart" should be in the \'orderable\' list.\n\nSince we now must choose "tart" as \'orderable\', we can\'t add "baklava" and "shawarma" as \'orderable\', because that would dissatisfy Mel, Wei, and Shan.\n\nHence, "baklava" and "shawarma" go into the \'not_orderable\' list, because it satisfies some people who dislike them and not including them in the \'orderable\' list doesn\'t make anyone unhappy since their other likes can be accommodated.\n\nNow, we further see that "spaghetti" is liked by some and also disliked by many. However, we have many alternatives for those who like "spaghetti" (for instance, those who like "spaghetti" also like either "tart" or "fries" or "frittata" which we haven\'t placed yet), so we can consider placing "spaghetti" in \'not_orderable\'. This will satisfy all those who dislike "spaghetti."\n\nAs for "fries", they are liked by many and not as frequently disliked as other items. Therefore, we can place "fries" in \'orderable\'.\n\nLet\'s put "frittata" in the \'orderable\' list to satisfy those who like it.\n\nWhat\'s left is "burrito". When we look at the list, we see that fewer people are satisfied by including "burrito" in the \'orderable\' list (and there are alternatives for some who like it such as "frittata" and "fries" that have already been included). Therefore, we can safely put "burrito" in the \'not_orderable\' list.\n\nIn summary, to satisfy everyone:\n\n\'Orderable\': "tart", "fries", "frittata"\n\n\'Not_orderable\': "baklava", "shawarma", "spaghetti", "burrito"\n\nLet\'s output these in Python list format as requested:\n\n```\norderable=[\'tart\', \'fries\', \'frittata\'], not_orderable=[\'baklava\', \'shawarma\', \'spaghetti\', \'burrito\']\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 1243, 'num_completion_tokens': 833}
