s. We have a provisional decision about tiramisu (not_orderable to satisfy many dislikers) and a leaning towards putting mousse on the 'not_orderable' list too.\n\nLet's start by putting poke ('orderable') and mousse ('not_orderable') in their respective preliminary positions, which will satisfy the following people:\n\nSatisfied by poke being 'orderable': Aarav, Eli, Mia, Fay, Jaya, Jim, Ping, Mina, Wes, Kit, Diya\nSatisfied by mousse being 'not_orderable': Mei, Eli, Ava, Fay, Zac, Dan, Jim, Wes, Nic, Kit\n\nNow let's see who's left and whether tiramisu or sorbet can satisfy them:\n\nTiramisu as 'not_orderable' would satisfy Zoe, Pam, Jaya, Zac, Nic, Kai, Kit, and Chao.\n\nNow, let's review the remaining people and their preferences to ensure everyone is satisfied:\n\n- Mei, Ava: Like tiramisu but it’s in our 'not_orderable', dislike poke but it’s in our 'orderable'. They would not be satisfied yet.\n- Aarav: Satisfied by poke being 'orderable'.\n- Eli: Likes tiramisu and poke, dislikes mousse. Satisfied.\n- Fay: Likes poke and tiramisu, dislikes mousse. Satisfied.\n- Mia: Satisfied by poke. \n- Zoe, Pam, Jaya, Zac, Nic, Kai, Kit: Would be satisfied by tiramisu being 'not_orderable'.\n- Dan: Likes sorbet, dislikes tiramisu and mousse. Not satisfied yet, but could be with sorbet 'orderable'.\n- Jim: Satisfied by poke.\n- Naina: Dislike mousse and poke, likes sorbet. Would also be satisfied with sorbet 'orderable'.\n- Lan, Kim, Cy: Like mousse and sorbet but dislike poke which is 'orderable'. They need sorbet to be 'orderable' to be satisfied.\n- Ping: Satisfied by poke.\n- Mina, Wes: Satisfied by poke.\n- Diya: Likes all three poke, sorbet, and tiramisu. Satisfied either way.\n\nTo satisfy everyone, we need to add sorbet to 'orderable' list. This way everyone will have at least one liked item in 'orderable' or one disliked item in 'not_orderable'.\n\nTallying up, all participants will be satisfied with this final distribution:\n\n'Orderable': poke, sorbet\n'Not_orderable': mousse, tiramisu\n\nHere is the Python representation:\n\n```python\norderable=['poke', 'sorbet']\nnot_orderable=['mousse', 'tiramisu']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 527, 'num_completion_tokens': 1227}
