rav. Disliked by Jon, Kai, Pam, Gia, Ansh, Val, Cal, Diya, Ben, and Rex.\n- Ratatouille: Liked by Riya, Lou, Rob, Pam, Gia, Gen, Amy, Cy, Zara, Ansh, Raj, Nic, Aarav, Tia, Lee, Abe, and Qi. Disliked by Jon, Kai, Ty, Ying, Sue, Val, Cal, Diya, Ben, and Zoe.\n- Pie: Liked by Jon, Rob, Gia, Ravi, Zara, Amy, Zoe, Diya, Joy, Nic, Aarav, Tia, Lee, Qi, Rex, and Abe. Disliked by Riya, Lou, Pam, Gen, Cy, Ty, Ansh, Raj, Sue, Val, Cal, Ying, and Ben.\n\nSince Kai, Val, Cal, and Ben dislike all three food items, in order to satisfy them at least one of these items must be placed in the 'not_orderable' list. But every food item is on somebody’s liked list as well, which means that no matter what item we place in the 'not_orderable' list, someone who likes it will not be satisfied since that item is not in the orderable list.\n\nThus, based on the satisfaction criteria, it is impossible to satisfy all participants, and no such combination exists. Therefore, the output should be empty lists for both 'orderable' and 'not_orderable'.\n\n<orderable=[], not_orderable=[]>", 'num_prompt_tokens': 603, 'num_completion_tokens': 377}
