o dislike them, leaving Mina needing something she likes to be orderable.\n6. Since Mina dislikes Pie and Salad, we can add Salad to the 'orderable' list to satisfy Arun, Vic, and Ben.\n7. At this point, everyone has at least one liked item in the 'orderable' list or one disliked item in the 'not_orderable' list.\n\nOrderable list:\n- Tandoori: Satisfies Arun, Riya, Kai, Jun, Ken\n- Pie: Satisfies Lin, Vic\n- Salad: Satisfies Arun, Vic, Ben, and presumably this also satisfies Mina since she has no further likes and one of her dislikes (Vegetables) is not orderable.\n\nNot orderable list:\n- Kebab: Satisfies Arun, Vic, Ken\n- Vegetables: Satisfies Lin, Riya, May, Ken\n\nWe've now made a list that satisfies everyone's preferences according to the given criteria. Let's display them in Python code format:\n\n```python\norderable=['tandoori', 'pie', 'salad']\nnot_orderable=['kebab', 'vegetables']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 325, 'num_completion_tokens': 602}
