nd are not the only liked items for people who dislike them.\n\nStill, due to the complex interplays of likes and dislikes, and without further constraints, we immediately run into conflicts which cannot be resolved while satisfying all requirements.\n\nConsidering the given preferences, there are competitive interests in popular items like baklava, udon, pancakes, frittata, and mousse which are liked by many but also disliked by some - often as the only disliked item.\n\nAfter reviewing the likes and dislikes, it's evident that it is impossible to satisfy all individuals based on the given criteria. Therefore, we must output empty lists for both 'orderable' and 'not_orderable'.\n\nOutputting the solution in Python code:\n```python\norderable = []\nnot_orderable = []\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 1312, 'num_completion_tokens': 985}
