al others.\n- Udon is disliked by Lee (when considering other likes), Rina, Arun, Pam, Eli, Tao, Sid, and Du.\n- Burger is disliked by Val, Arun, Pam, Ana, Ru, Du, and Diya.\n- Soup is disliked by Sue, Rina, Val, and Pam.\n- Gelato is disliked by Lin, Sal, Anil, Ru, Sid, and Mina.\n- Churros are disliked by Sue, Val, Arun, Tao, Anil, and Sid.\n\nThe most commonly disliked item is pho, making it an ideal candidate for the `not_orderable` list. This will immediately satisfy many people who dislike pho. We'll try to place pho in the `not_orderable` list to start:\n\n`not_orderable = ['pho']`\n\nNext, we need at least one liked item from each person in the `orderable` list. To minimize conflicts, we should choose items that are not mentioned as dislikes by others. We can start with items that are liked by several people and not disliked by anyone or disliked the least:\n\n- Guacamole is liked by multiple people (Lee, Sal, Taj, Kit) and is not listed as a dislike.\n- Burger is liked by multiple people (Sue, Rina, Liz, Fay, Eli, Taj, Tom), but it is disliked by some, so we need to be careful with this choice.\n- Soup is liked by multiple people (Lin, Jun, Fay, Diya, May, Feng), but disliked by several as well, so it might not be a good choice.\n- Churros are liked by Jun, Liz, Jay, and Mina, and disliked by a few; they are a possible choice but need to be checked against other preferences.\n- Gelato is liked by multiple people (Jun, Liz, Ana), but disliked by several too.\n\nSince guacamole is liked by many and not disliked by anyone, we can add it to the `orderable` list first:\n\n`orderable = ['guacamole']`\n\nNext, let's add one liked food item for each remaining individual, without conflicting with dislikes:\n\n- Jun has churros and gelato liked; out of which churros will satisfy the most people without causing issues.\n- Lin likes soup, and since it's only disliked by four people, we could consider it, but we should hold off in case we can find a better option as it 