y, Meg)\n- kimchi: 4 (from Ana, Mina, Aarav, Isha)\n- cheese: 2 (from Joy, Rohan)\n- kebab: 3 (from Joy, Jaya, Tom)\n- omelette: 4 (from Val, Rohan, Aarav, Pat)\n- ravioli: 3 (from Val, Xan, Rina)\n- risotto: 3 (from Mina, Aarav, Pat)\n\nLet\'s sort these items into potential \'orderable\' and \'not_orderable\' based on the majority consensus:\n\nLikely \'orderable\':\n- cheese (3 likes vs 2 dislikes)\n- brownies (3 likes vs 3 dislikes, but Tom likes, and his only other like, kebab, is disliked)\n- omelette (2 likes vs 4 dislikes, but potential to satisfy Isha and Jon)\n\nLikely \'not_orderable\':\n- kimchi (2 likes vs 4 dislikes)\n- kebab (2 likes vs 3 dislikes, but Val likes and dislikes both ravioli and omelette)\n- ravioli (1 like vs 3 dislikes)\n- risotto (1 like vs 3 dislikes)\n\nNow, let\'s satisfy each individual based on the "satisfaction criteria":\n\nAna: Likes ravioli (not orderable due to more dislikes than likes). Dislikes brownies, kimchi (both could be not_orderable). If kimchi is on \'not_orderable\', satisfaction is met since dislikes override likes.\nJoy: Dislikes cheese, brownies, kebab (cheese can be orderable, brownies potentially orderable, kebab likely not_orderable). Joy can be satisfied if either cheese or brownies is orderable and kebab is not_orderable.\nVal: Likes kebab (not_orderable). Dislikes omelette, ravioli (both can be not_orderable). Satisfied with kebab being not_orderable.\nMeg: Likes cheese, kimchi (cheese can be orderable, kimchi likely not_orderable). Dislikes brownies (brownies can be orderable). Satisfied with cheese being orderable.\nJaya: Likes brownies, cheese (both can be orderable). Dislikes kebab (not_orderable). Satisfied with cheese or brownies being orderable and kebab being not_orderable.\nRohan: Dislikes omelette, cheese, brownies (omelette and cheese can both be orderable, brownies potentially orderable). Satisfied as long as cheese isn\'t the only thing on the orderable list.\nMina: Likes kebab (not_orderable)