rderable' and 'not_orderable' items:\n\n- Any person who likes kebab, fries, quiche, or gelato should be satisfied if those items are orderable.\n- Anyone who dislikes hummus, ratatouille, or salad should be satisfied since those items are not orderable.\n\nSince kebab is on our 'orderable' list and no participant who dislikes kebab doesn't have another like or dislike to satisfy them, we should be fine. The same logic is applied for fries, quiche, and gelato on this list. On the 'not_orderable' side, participants who dislike hummus, ratatouille, or salad have other likes or dislikes to ensure their satisfaction.\n\nAfter ensuring that all participants are satisfied by these lists, we can confirm our solution:\n\norderable=['kebab', 'fries', 'quiche', 'gelato'], not_orderable=['hummus', 'ratatouille', 'salad']", 'num_prompt_tokens': 1326, 'num_completion_tokens': 952}
