s are all in "not_orderable" or dislikes are not in "not_orderable", and they don\'t have any dislikes in "orderable", then we cannot satisfy everyone and might have to rearrange the lists.\n\nAfter trying different combinations and attempting to satisfy everyone\'s preferences, it\'s clear that the constraints are too conflicting, meaning it\'s impossible to construct "orderable" and "not_orderable" lists that will satisfy all participants. Each time an item is placed into one list to satisfy one person, it causes a conflict with another.\n\nAs such, we have to output empty lists for both `orderable` and `not_orderable`.\n\nFinal solution:\n```python\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 1116, 'num_completion_tokens': 1007}
