m they dislike in the \'orderable\' list.  \n\nGiven that "omelette" is already on the \'not_orderable\' list, people who dislike "pho," "cake," and "waffles" are already satisfied since at least one item they dislike is not on the orderable list.\n\nTo confirm, let\'s make sure everyone who likes "pho" doesn\'t have a problem with other liking and no one dislikes "pho" alone:\n\n- Gia, Sol, Rob, Pia, Dot, Xiu, Chao, Eli, Om, Ben, Rex, Aarav, Hu, and Mina all like "pho" and don\'t dislike items that others like exclusively.\n- Nic, Lan, and Ray all dislike "pho," but they also dislike "waffles" and "curry," which we are not including in the \'orderable\' list because they are also disliked by others.\n\nTherefore, the \'orderable\' list will have "pho," and the \'not_orderable\' list will have "omelette." No other items should be added because they are liked and disliked by different participants, which doesn\'t allow us to find a combination that satisfies all criteria.\n\nThe final solution is:\n```python\norderable = [\'pho\'], not_orderable = [\'omelette\']\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 790, 'num_completion_tokens': 603}
