_orderable\'.\n\nSince we need to satisfy everyone, we\'re looking for food items that are liked by some of the group but disliked by none as \'orderable\', and ones that are disliked by some of the group but liked by none as \'not_orderable\'.\n\nFrom the above preferences, we can see that:\n\n- "gelato" is liked by some (Wei, Jan, Nic, Anil, Val, Neil, Eva, Zara) and not disliked by anyone else.\n- "shrimps" is problematic because it\'s liked by many but also disliked by many.\n- "custard" is liked by some (Kavi, Liz, Mel, Ron) and not disliked by anyone else.\n- "udon" is also problematic because it\'s liked by some (Veer, Ty, Mel, Max, Xiu, Lei, Ava) but disliked by others.\n- "tacos" are liked by several (Rina, Tao, Ru, Hal, Lia, Lin, Nita, Pat, Eli, Eva) and not disliked by anyone.\n- "caramel" is problematic because it\'s liked by many but also disliked by others.\n\nNow that gelato, custard and tacos can be ordered (since they\'re liked and not disliked), let\'s see if this arrangement leaves anyone unsatisfied. If everyone is satisfied with gelato, custard or tacos being orderable, then all others not explicitly liked can be \'not_orderable\'.\n\nLooking through the preferences, it\'s clear that no one has a problem with gelato, custard, and tacos being orderable. Now we can assign everything else that is not liked to the \'not_orderable\' list.\n\nNow let\'s move the other items to \'not_orderable\':\n\n- "kimchi" is disliked by some (Ken, Chao, Veer, Ula, Hui, Gen, Ada, Wes, Hal, Jaya, Arun, Pia) and not absolutely required by others since they have other likes which are orderable.\n- "shrimps" is disliked by many and liked by many, but since we already have orderable items to satisfy everyone who likes shrimp, it can be not orderable.\n- "udon" is disliked by several people and liked by some, but again, since we have other orderable items that satisfy the people who like udon\'s preferences, we can place udon in not orderable.\n- "caramel" is also liked and disliked, but since we have other items satisfying those who like caramel, it can also go into not_orderable.\n\nLastly, we review everyone\'s preferences to ensure that each person has at least one liked item or one disliked item on the correct list.\n\nSince it appears that all people can be satisfied with the arrangement of \'gelato\', \'custard\', and \'tacos\' in \'orderable\' and the remaining items \'kimchi\', \'shrimps\', \'udon\', \'caramel\' in \'not_orderable\', we have our solution.\n\nTherefore, after reviewing all preferences and ensuring that everyone is satisfied, we can conclude with the following lists:\n\n```python\norderable=[\'gelato\', \'custard\', \'tacos\']\nnot_orderable=[\'kimchi\', \'shrimps\', \'udon\', \'caramel\']\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 953, 'num_completion_tokens': 838}
