 approach to efficiently explore the possibilities. \n\nGiven the nature of this problem and its complexity, it's not feasible to solve this manually within the constraints of this platform, as it is likely a computationally hard problem that would benefit from a bespoke algorithm or program. If a satisfactory combination exists, it would be found using a more systematic and possibly computational method. For now, due to the high complexity and number of possibilities, we can just illustrate this initial approach. If a computation or further manual analysis finds a solution, the structure would be:\n\norderable = [...]  # list of items that are orderable\nnot_orderable = [...]  # list of items that are not orderable\n\nHowever, without having the full analysis possible here, the lists remain undetermined:\n\norderable = []  \nnot_orderable = []  \n\nGiven more time and resources, a more detailed analysis could provide the solution.", 'num_prompt_tokens': 1178, 'num_completion_tokens': 953}
