st, since they are crucial in ensuring that no one is unsatisfied:\n\nEveryone who dislikes "Wonton": Arun, Yue\nEveryone who dislikes "Udon": Diya, Rohan, Ping, Vic, Val, Xiu\nEveryone who dislikes "Custard": Diya, Lin, Yan, Val\n\nNone of the dislikes are unanimous, so we can\'t simply put any item in the \'not_orderable\' list outright.\n\nHowever, "Arun" and "Yue" dislike all three items. To satisfy them, we must put all three on either list, but this is not possible since item 3 (No item can appear on both lists). Hence, it is not possible to meet the criteria for a list that satisfies everyone. \n\nTherefore, our solution as per the given criteria must be to output empty lists for both:\n\n```python\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 360, 'num_completion_tokens': 495}
