o it also cannot be included.\n- Lasagna, being liked by some and disliked by others, is also not a good option.\n- Couscous is liked by many but disliked by some.\n- Spaghetti is liked by some but disliked by others.\n- Macaron is liked by many but disliked by some, so it cannot be included.\n\nThis means we cannot find a single food item to put in the 'orderable' list that isn't disliked by at least one person, and cannot find a single item to put in the 'not_orderable' list that isn't liked by at least one person.\n\nTherefore, it is not possible to create two distinct lists of 'orderable' and 'not_orderable' items where all participants are satisfied according to the given rules. Our output will be:\n\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n\nThis complex scenario with multiple likes and dislikes overlapping means there is no combination of 'orderable' and 'not_orderable' foods that would satisfy everyone’s food preferences.", 'num_prompt_tokens': 1146, 'num_completion_tokens': 641}
