obster and his only like is pizza, so we must ensure that lobster is not in \'orderable\' to keep him satisfied. Since other people like lobster, it cannot go into \'not_orderable\' either, yet those who like lobster (Jaya, Hal, Liv, Jay, Vic, Taj, Ned, Joy, Amy, and Ned) are satisfied with pizza.\n\nUp to now, it looks like this satisfies all participants. \n\nNow to check if there are remaining conflicts amongst the rests or additional preferences where we must ensure at least one like on the orderable list or one dislike on the not_orderable list. Here\'s a detailed look at the remaining items:\n\nVegetables, hummus, risotto, paneer, and bruschetta are still left, but deciding where they go is tough. \n\n- Vegetables can\'t go in \'not_orderable\' because the like group (Pam, Hui, Jay, Mia, Om, Kavi) doesn\'t have enough other likes/dislikes based on the existing \'orderable\' and \'not_orderable\'.\n- Hummus is liked by many but placing it in either list is impossible due to conflicting likes and dislikes.\n- Risotto is liked by many and also has conflict since placing it in \'orderable\' would disappoint Chao, Nita, Ula, Gen, etc., and \'not_orderable\' would disappoint its likers.\n- Paneer can\'t go into \'not_orderable\' as its likers like May, Tara, Sol, Sky, Bea, Rohan, Ava, Ana, and Dot – no other satisfying elements on the \'orderable\' or \'not_orderable\' lists.\n- Bruschetta being in \'orderable\' would again cause issues with its dislikers.\n\nAfter analyzing all remaining items, we realize there\'s no clear path to satisfy everyone because some participants\' dislikes would force an item into \'not_orderable\', but other participants\' likes would demand it to be \'orderable\' for satisfaction.\n\nSince no item can appear on both lists, and we cannot identify a conflict-free combination, the final solution is that both lists should remain empty, as there is no combination that satisfies all participants based on the given criteria.\n\nHence, the final lists will be:\n\n```python\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 833, 'num_completion_tokens': 1576}
