risotto. Bao: Likes espresso. Dislikes shrimps, wonton. Yan: Likes fries, tart. Dislikes risotto. Cal: Likes tart. Dislikes espresso, risotto. Liz: Dislikes risotto, espresso, pho. Ana: Likes pho. Dislikes wonton, tart. Nic: Likes tart, espresso. Dislikes shrimps. Ned: Likes tart. Dislikes pho, fries. Xiu: Likes fries. Dislikes pho, shrimps. Mel: Likes shrimps, wonton. Dislikes tart. ', 'menu_items': ['espresso', 'tart', 'pho', 'shrimps', 'risotto', 'fries', 'wonton'], 'gpt_out': "The process of determining the 'orderable' and 'not_orderable' lists will involve ensuring the satisfaction criteria for each individual in the group based on their likes and dislikes. We want to find at least one liked item for each person in the 'orderable' list and ensure any disliked item by someone appears in the 'not_orderable' list, all while no item appears on both lists and every participant is satisfied.\n\nFirst, we should check for any items that are unanimously disliked by all and can be safely put in the 'not_orderable' list. Similarly, we should find any items that are liked by at least one person and not disliked by anyone, which can be safely put in the 'orderable' list. However, in this case, there seems to be no such unanimously disliked or undisputed liked item.\n\nNext, let's find items that must be in the 'orderable' list because it's the only liked item for some people ('must-have' items) and those that everyone who likes them, also dislikes something else ('flexible' items).\n\n'Must-have' items:\n- Espresso: Sam, Tia, Mina, Bao, Nic like it and no one else dislikes it.\n- Shrimps: Everyone who likes shrimps dislikes something else too, so it's a 'flexible' item.\n- Pho: Everyone who likes pho dislikes something else too, so it's a 'flexible' item.\n- Wonton: Everyone who likes wonton dislikes something else too, so it's a 'flexible' item.\n- Tart: Everyone who likes tart dislikes something else too, so it's a 'flexible' item.\n- Risotto: Everyone who likes risotto dislikes something else too, so it's a 'flexible' item.\n- Fries: Everyone who likes fries dislikes something else too, so it's a 'flexible' item.\n\n'Flexible' items:\n- Shrimps, pho, wonton, tart, risotto, fries\n\nSince espresso is the only 'must-have' item, we can put it directly in the 'orderable' list:\n\n'Orderable': [espresso]\n\nNow we need to ensure everyone is satisfied by making sure at least one like for everyone appears in 'orderable' or one dislike appears in 'not_orderable'. Let us now look at dislikes to find items that can be placed in 'not_orderable' considering the already 'orderable' item.\n\n'Must-not-have' items (items that if not included in 'not_orderable' someone will be unsatisfied):\n- Wonton: Arun, Sam, Joe, May, Min, Eva, Veer, Meg, Leo, Bao, Ana\n- Fries: Arun, Zara, Chen, Sky, Li, Veer, Ned, Dan\n\nThese two items, wonton and fries, are the only ones that are disliked by people who do not have any other dislikes. They must be in 'not_orderable' to satisfy them:\n\n'Not_orderable': [wonton, fries]\n\nNow that we have espresso in 'orderable' and wonton and fries in 'not_orderable', every subsequent item must be checked to ensure it doesn't conflict with the satisfaction of those who have a remaining dislike or no liked item in 'orderable'.\n\nChecking remaining items to fulfill everyone's likes:\n- Shrimps: Can be ordered. No one with shrimps as the only like has an unresolved dislike, and those who dislike it (Sam, Mia, Hui, Ping, Bao, Nic, Wei, Xiu) have other likes or dislikes that are resolved.\n- Pho: Can be ordered. No one with pho as their single liked item has an unresolved dislike, and those who dislike it (Chao, Veer, Liz, Ned) have other likes or dislikes that are satisfied.\n- Tart: Cannot be ordered or it must be not ordered. Diya, Ping, Nita, Eva, and Rex have it as their only dislike, and they have no other liked item on the 'orderable' list yet.\n- Risotto: Cannot be ordered. Ivy, Joe, Arun, Ping, Aarav, Yan, and Cal have it as their only dislike, and they have not been satisfied by 'orderable' items yet.\n\nGiven that tart cannot be ordered because it is the single dislike for several individuals, it must go into the 'not_orderable' list to satisfy them. Risotto cannot be ordered for the same reason, and must also go into 'not_orderable'.\n\n'Not_orderable': [wonton, fries, tart, risotto]\n\nFinal 'Orderable' items (every person will have at least one item they like or a disliked item in the 'not_orderable' list):\n- Shrimps: It’s okay to order since it does not violate the satisfaction criteria and there's no conflict with the 'must-not-have' items.\n- Pho: It’s also okay to order for the same reason as shrimps.\n\nFinal Considerations:\n- The remaining items not mentioned can be included in 'orderable' as long as they do not conflict with the above lists.\n- Espresso has to be in 'orderable' to satisfy all who like it (since it's their only like for some).\n- Shrimps and pho can be added to 'orderable' as no one's satisfaction is dependent on these items not being ordered.\n\nThus:\n\n```python\norderable=['espresso', 'shrimps', 'pho']\nnot_orderable=['wonton', 'fries', 'tart', 'risotto']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 745, 'num_completion_tokens': 1171}
