aloo from the \'orderable\' list.\n- Everyone who likes ramen can still be satisfied because they all also like either fries, shrimps, or vindaloo.\n- Fries can be \'orderable\' without issue as it is liked by people who also like ramen or vindaloo.\n- Shrimps and vindaloo can be \'orderable\' since the people who dislike them have other options on the \'orderable\' list to satisfy them.\n\nLet\'s finalize the results:\n\n```python\norderable=["fries", "shrimps", "vindaloo"], not_orderable=["ramen"]\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 715, 'num_completion_tokens': 1050}
