o the 'not_orderable' list and see who would be satisfied:\n- Adding **kimchi** to 'not_orderable' would satisfy Neil, Wes, Mei, Ansh, Jaya, Tara, Ron, Ken, Qi, Ava, Hal, Sol, Pat, Diya, and Yue. It would not satisfy any person who likes **kimchi** (because it's readily satisfied by **lobster** in the 'orderable' list).\n\nNow we have to look at the remaining likings and dislikings:\n- **Mousse** is still tricky because it is both strongly liked and disliked, so let's keep it undecided for now.\n\nEveryone who likes **lobster** is satisfied, and those who dislike **kimchi** are satisfied. Let's look at those whose preferences included **sorbet** or **shrimps**, but now are unsatisfied since they dislike **lobster** and like **kimchi** which we proposed for 'not_orderable':\n\n- For **sorbet**, we have Kit, Ben, Tara, Min, Veer, Anil, Zac, and Chen - some of whom are already dissatisfied because they dislike **lobster**. \nHowever, placing **sorbet** into 'orderable' would offend Neil, Zac, Wes, Tao, Joy, Qi, and Sol, who all dislike **sorbet** but are satisfied with either **lobster** as orderable or **kimchi** as not_orderable. Since **sorbet** is disliked by individuals who are otherwise satisfied, it's best to leave **sorbet** out of the 'orderable' list. Therefore, it should be placed in 'not_orderable'.\n\n- For **shrimps**, we have Neil, Zac, Hal, Ansh, Ava, Tia, Rob, Gus, Naina, Yue, Pia, Ana, Tara, Veer, Ben, and Kavi - some of whom are already dissatisfied because they dislike **lobster**, but adding **shrimps** to 'not_orderable' will satisfy them without dissatisfying any currently satisfied individuals.\n\nAt this stage, we satisfy everyone's preferences by placing **lobster** in 'orderable', **kimchi** and **sorbet** in 'not_orderable', and adding **shrimps** to 'not_orderable' makes sure we don't dissatisfy anybody else.\n\n'Mousse' is still left. If it is placed in 'orderable', then anyone who dislikes mousse but likes lobster (Mei, Ansh, Ken, Qi, Pat