\n4. Zan, Ken and Wei just got satisfied from our 'orderable' decision, so we don't have to worry about their only likes.\n\nConsidering dislikes, we realize that some items can never be on the 'orderable' list because placing them on the list would dissatisfy someone who only has that single dislike.\n\n1. Kimchi is disliked by Tara, Wes, Ying, Lin, Nic, Ray, Rex, and Ty and also by Pam who likes bread which we've placed it on 'orderable'. Only Rina, Wei, Ru, Max, Tom and Anil like Kimchi but Kimchi is the only item Anil likes. This indicates that Kimchi must be placed on the 'orderable' list to satisfy Anil. Thus, satisfyingly disliked by Tara, Wes, Ying, Lin, Nic, Ray, Rex, Ty and Pam which means satisfying all of them too.\n\n2. Custard is disliked by Tara, Nita, Riya, Lei, Ray, Lin, Qi, Ying, and Chao. Riya and Joy like Custard but Joy also likes Paneer. We will now see if paneer is forced on either list.\n\nPaneer is disliked by Wes, Sol, Rina, Nic, Ray, Ty, Jim, Xiu, Lei, Wei and Ben. Jim, Ty and Xiu only have dislikes including paneer, so they will be satisfied if paneer is not on the 'orderable' list. Riya and Joy like Paneer and also like Custard for Joy it's the only remain and for Riya who also like Custard but since Joy likes also paneer that cannot be in 'orderable', Custard which is the only choice has to be on 'orderable'. This will satisfy also Om who likes custard and dislikes Kimchi that is on 'orderable' list.\n\n3. Now when paneer is not in 'orderable' or 'not_orderable' list, Ken is satisfied due to his disliking of nachos and bread.\n\n4. Nita who likes pancakes and cheese but dislikes custard, now she already satisfied because custard is on 'orderable'.\n\n5. Nachos is disliked by Zan, Geet, Ying, Li and Hui. Chao who has no fondness left, he does not like bread and custard they are placed on 'orderable' while pancakes is also in liked by others. So nachos has to be in 'orderable' for him to get satisfied.\n\nAt this point, we can calculate who are left:\n- Zan: Likes cheese, which Ken dislikes. Since Zan can't be satisfied by bread, but cheese is the only item he likes left and Ken is already satisfied, we place cheese on the 'orderable' list.\n- Ben likes nachos and custard and both are in 'orderable'.\n- Geet likes bread and dislikes pancakes and nachos. Both disliked are already on 'orderable' list and bread is on 'orderable' the same with Leo and Pam.\n- Rohan likes cheese and paneer and dislikes pancakes. Cheese is already in 'orderable', pancakes with all other dislikes from people who likes them can't be put in 'not_orderable'.\n- Li likes nachos and dislikes pancakes as main concerns both like and dislike is on proper list.\n- Max likes kimchi and custard. Both are in 'orderable'.\n- Tom and Qi likes bread which is already in 'orderable' but they also dislikes custard which is also in 'orderable'. \n\nAll participants are now satisfied with the existing 'orderable' and not 'not_orderable' any item. \n\nFinal lists:\n- Orderable: bread, kimchi, custard, cheese, nachos\n- Not orderable: None\n\nIn python code format:\n```python\norderable=['bread', 'kimchi', 'custard', 'cheese', 'nachos'], not_orderable=[]\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 639, 'num_completion_tokens': 1222}
