the biggest group, cheese can go to 'not_orderable' to satisfy the rest.\n\nSo, the 'orderable' list will have ravioli, which is liked by the majority. The 'not_orderable' list will have cheese and sorbet, which are each disliked by a sufficient number of individuals who like ravioli as well as those who dislike ravioli but like sorbet.\n\nFinal solution:\n```python\norderable=['ravioli'], not_orderable=['cheese', 'sorbet']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 652, 'num_completion_tokens': 714}
