ly liked item (Nita likes it but also likes waffles and paneer).\n- Sorbet: Disliked by Aarav, Ned, Ping, Max. The only people who only like sorbet and no other items are Val, but Val also dislikes ravioli and pancakes.\n\nTherefore, 'Shrimps' and 'Gelato' can be safely placed in the 'not_orderable' list. Sorbet is liked by some but is the sole liked item for no one.\n\nNext, we need to find at least one liked item for each person that isn't also disliked by someone else, which can be quite challenging.\n\nLet's see if there are any items that everyone who likes them, likes nothing else:\n\n- Paneer: Liked by Jay, Nita, Gia, Liv, Gen but disliked by Ping, Lei, and Max. It cannot be the sole orderable item because it is also disliked, but we'll keep it in mind.\n- Omelette: Liked by Jay, Kim, Jon, Ty, Gia but disliked by Qi, Aarav, Om, Gen, Lin. It cannot be the sole orderable item for the same reason as above.\n\nReviewing the provided preferences, there seems to be no single liked food item that isn't disliked by someone else, so our approach to satisfying everyone will need to involve multiple items.\n\nWe know for certain that:\n- Shrimps and Gelato can be placed in 'not_orderable' as no one likes them.\n\nWe also need to address overlaps in dislikes; for example, Aarav dislikes Gelato, Sorbet, and Omelette, all of which are liked by at least one person. Since Gelato is already not orderable, we need to keep either Sorbet or Omelette orderable to satisfy Aarav. However, Omelette is also disliked by others and necessary to satisfy Jon and Gia, who do not share other likes, so it must be orderable. Therefore, Sorbet must not be orderable to meet the criteria for Aarav, as Omelette will be orderable to satisfy Jon and Gia.\n\nConsidering this, if Omelette is orderable, Qi, Om, and Lin will be unsatisfied. Since Qi also likes Waffles, Lin likes Ravioli, and Om's only like is Ravioli, Waffles and Ravioli can be added to orderable to ensure their satisfaction. However, since Abe dislikes Ravioli, he would require Waffles to be orderable, which is compatible with Qi's satisfaction.\n\nWith Waffles, Omelette, and Ravioli in the orderable list, we satisfy most of the individuals, except for Ping, who dislikes both Paneer and Ravioli. Since there are no other items Ping likes, we cannot satisfy everyone's preferences with the given criteria. Ty and Val also have Sorbet as their like, but it's not their only like. Ty also likes Omelette and Pancakes, and Val dislikes Ravioli and Pancakes.\n\nTherefore, it's impossible to satisfy everyone according to the criteria. Thus the output will be empty lists for both 'orderable' and 'not_orderable'.\n\nThe final output is:\n```python\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 546, 'num_completion_tokens': 788}
