). Can't be 'not_orderable' because it is liked by many, placing it in 'orderable' will dissatisfy all those who dislike it.\n\n**Macaron**: Disliked by Arun, Leo, Ada, Ana, Bao, and liked by Bea, Ben, Rob, Min, Ron, Kim, Diya. Can't be 'not_orderable' because it is liked by many, placing it in 'orderable' will dissatisfy all those who dislike it.\n\n**Churros**: Disliked by Bea, Ben, Arun, Min, Ron, Ivy, Jon, Raj, Sid; and liked by Leo, Rob, Kim, Diya, Dan, Vic. Due to the number of dislikes, we may consider placing churros in 'not_orderable' if possible, since not as many people like it compared to kebab and macaron.\n\nThe 'not_orderable' list can include churros, as Leo and Vic like churros but dislike the other two items, therefore they would be satisfied by churros being 'not_orderable'. This implies that Dan, who likes kebab and churros but dislikes macaron, can also be satisfied if we put kebab in the 'orderable' list. Kim and Diya both like macaron and churros, and dislike kebab, so they would be satisfied with churros in 'not_orderable' and macaron in 'orderable'. Rob likes all three, so they can be satisfied with either kebab or macaron in 'orderable'. \n\nLet's create tentative lists based on this consideration:\n\n**orderable**: kebab, macaron\n**not_orderable**: churros\n\nIf we add kebab and macaron to 'orderable' and churros to 'not_orderable', we satisfy the following:\n\n- Those who dislike churros are satisfied with churros in 'not_orderable'.\n- Bea, Ben, and Rob are satisfied with either kebab or macaron in 'orderable'.\n- Leo, Vic, and Dan are satisfied with churros in 'not_orderable' and kebab in 'orderable'.\n- Kim and Diya are satisfied with churros in 'not_orderable' and macaron in 'orderable'.\n- Min and Ron are satisfied with macaron in 'orderable'.\n- Ivy, Jon, Raj, and Sid are satisfied with kebab in 'orderable'.\n\nNow to check the others:\n\n- Arun, Ada, Ana, Bao all dislike all three items, hence they will be satisfied with churros in 'not_orderable'.\n\nIt appears we have found a combination that satisfies everyone. Let's output this combination as requested:\n\n```python\norderable=['kebab', 'macaron'], not_orderable=['churros']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 460, 'num_completion_tokens': 780}
