 of the items they like must be in the 'orderable' list or ravioli in the 'not_orderable'. Pam likes vegetables and caramel, Liz likes vegetables, so we might still find a solution here.\n- To satisfy Pat, who dislikes frittata, ravioli, and custard, and Lin, who dislikes caramel, at least one of the items Pat likes and one that Lin likes must be in 'orderable', but since they do not like anything common and without dislike, we cannot resolve this contradiciton. This means we immediately know a satisfactory combination is impossible.\n\nThe group's preferences are too diverse to find a solution that works for everyone. Therefore, both lists will be empty:\n\n```python\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 535, 'num_completion_tokens': 715}
