urger, roti\n- Vic: vegetables, burger\n- Li: wonton, roti\n- Joy: roti, vegetables\n- Ray: doughnut, pizza\n- Gen: pizza, wonton\n- Ava: doughnut, pizza\n\nNext, we will try to identify an item that every person that dislikes it also have a liked item that can compensate for it, and then make the item not orderable, because this will reduce the complexity as we eliminate disliked items as blockers effectively. \n\nGiven this, the key dislikes to consider making 'not_orderable' appear to be the following:\n- Pizza is disliked by Ron, Joe, Jon, Kavi, Ray, Gen, Ava and all of them have other liked foods that are not disliked by somebody who likes pizza (Li). So, we can put pizza in 'not_orderable'.\n- Burger is disliked by Nita, Rohan, Jon and Vic and all of them have other liked foods that are not disliked by somebody who likes burger (Ron, Tom, Joe, May, Ray). We can also place burger in 'not_orderable'.\n- Doughnut is disliked by Mina, Ben, Ivy, Ava and these are the only ones disliking doughnut, but all have other liked foods, so this can also be made not_orderable.\n\nNow all these people will be satisfied by 'not_orderable' items thus no longer blocking the foods they dislike. With those placed in 'not_orderable', we can consider the rest:\n\n- Ron is now satisfied (dislikes pizza; pizza is 'not_orderable')\n- Nita will need roti or vegetables to be satisfied (dislikes burger; burger is 'not_orderable')\n- Tom will need doughnut or burger to be satisfied, doughnut is 'not_orderable' so he is satisfied too\n- Rohan is satisfied with vegetables in 'orderable' (dislikes burger and roti, burger is 'not_orderable')\n- Joe is now satisfied since he dislikes pizza and it's 'not_orderable'\n- Mina needs roti or wonton, since doughnut is 'not_orderable'\n- Ben will need vegetables as both disliked items are 'not_orderable'\n- Jon will need doughnut in 'orderable' but it's 'not_orderable' so he is satisfied\n- May is satisfied by having burger 'not_orderable'\n- Kavi will need doughnut or wonton; doughnut is 'not_orderable'\n- Ivy needs roti as both burger and doughnut are 'not_orderable'\n- Eli is satisfied by having doughnut and burger 'not_orderable'\n- Vic needs roti as burger is 'not_orderable' and he dislikes vegetables\n- Li will need pizza but it's 'not_orderable' so he can't be satisfied.\n- Joy needs wonton as other liked items are 'not_orderable' or disliked by someone else\n- Ray is satisfied by having burger and pizza 'not_orderable'\n- Gen is also satisfied by having doughnut and pizza 'not_orderable'\n- Ava is satisfied by having vegetables since doughnut and pizza are 'not_orderable'\n\nLi cannot be satisfied since his only liked item, pizza, is 'not_orderable' and all remaining potential 'orderable' items are blocked by someone's dislike.\n\nSince Li's preference prevents us from making a list that includes every person being satisfied, the final result is that no such combination of 'orderable' and 'not_orderable' lists exists.\n\nTherefore, the output is:\n```\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 422, 'num_completion_tokens': 974}
