Yue, Abe, Kai, Jun, Mel, Riya, Ru, Neil, Jaya, Lex) either likes ramen or tart or both.\n- Everyone who dislikes ramen (Ray, Yan, Wes, Nita, Bo, Rohan, Mel, Ru, Sam, Bao) either likes guacamole or tart or both.\n- Everyone who dislikes tart (Ray, Yan, Wes, Nita, Bo, Rohan, Mel, Ru, Neil, Jaya, Veer, Lex) either likes guacamole or ramen or both.\n\nNext, we can see if anyone universally dislikes one of the dishes, which would mean it would have to be in the 'not_orderable' list to satisfy that person. We find that Mel, Ru, and Riya dislike all three dishes. For them to be satisfied, at least one of the dishes they dislike must be in 'not_orderable', but this could potentially clash with someone else's preferences.\n\nWe also note that not a single person dislikes only guacamole and nothing else; everyone who dislikes guacamole also dislikes at least one other dish. Therefore, placing guacamole on the 'orderable' list will not by itself cause dissatisfaction as a result of a clash in the 'not_orderable' list and will satisfy those who like it.\n\nTo ensure the maximum number of people are satisfied, let's first put guacamole in 'orderable' since a high proportion of individuals like it.\n\nNow, we need to check ramen and tart. If we put ramen in 'orderable', Yue, Abe, Kai, Jun, Mel, Riya, Ru, Neil, Jaya, and Lex will not be satisfied, but Mel, Riya, and Ru can be satisfied by putting tart in 'not_orderable'. We also notice that all the people who dislike tart like either ramen or guacamole, so placing tart in 'not_orderable' will not displease anyone by itself.\n\nGiven this, it looks like we can place tart in 'not_orderable' and guacamole in 'orderable'. This combination satisfies everyone because:\n\n- All guacamole lovers are happy because guacamole is 'orderable'.\n- All tart dislikers are happy because tart is 'not_orderable'.\n- All ramen dislikers have either guacamole or tart 'orderable' except Mel, Riya, and Ru, who are satisfied having tart in 'not_orderable'.\n- All who only like ramen or tart (and dislike the other dishes) are also satisfied with guacamole.\n- Mel, Riya, and Ru are appeased by having tart in 'not_orderable'.\n\nSo our final lists are:\norderable = ['guacamole']\nnot_orderable = ['tart']\n\nNo one likes just ramen, so there's no need to include it in 'orderable' to satisfy anyone. Now let's write these lists in Python code format:\n\n```python\norderable=['guacamole'], not_orderable=['tart']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 603, 'num_completion_tokens': 679}
