 Amy, Nic, Min, and Ivy would be unsatisfied. Hence, muffins must be *not_orderable*.\n\nLet\'s check if this satisfies everyone:\n\n- Those who like hummus are satisfied because it\'s orderable.\n- Those who dislike kebab are satisfied because it\'s not_orderable.\n- Those who like custard are satisfied because it\'s orderable.\n- Those who dislike muffins are satisfied because it\'s not_orderable.\n\nNo one has muffins as a like without having at least custard or hummus as another like, and no one has custard as a dislike without also disliking kebab or muffins. This combination should theoretically satisfy everyone.\n\nTherefore, our *orderable* list will have hummus and custard, and our *not_orderable* list will have kebab and muffins.\n\nHere is the final solution in Python format:\n\n```python\norderable = ["hummus", "custard"]\nnot_orderable = ["kebab", "muffins"]\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 531, 'num_completion_tokens': 917}
