s some individuals dislike what others like):\n\n- Gelato is liked by many but also disliked by many.\n- Espresso is liked by many but also disliked by many.\n- Macaron is liked by some but also disliked by many.\n- Tiramisu is liked by some but also disliked by many.\n- Korma is liked by many and disliked by fewer than gelato or espresso.\n\nDue to the polarized opinions on gelato, espresso, and macaron, they are not ideal candidates for 'orderable'. Tiramisu is also contentious, so we are left with korma, which seems like a potential item for the 'orderable' list.\n\nPlacing korma on 'orderable' would satisfy:\n\n- Wes, Dan, Tim, Kai, Geet, Kit, Abe, Tara, Bea, Cal, Mia, Bo, Veer, Sol, Sue, Neil, Jun, and Jun as they like korma and have no conflicting dislikes according to this choice.\n- Chen, Ping, Kim, Riya as they do not dislike korma, so their satisfaction must come from 'not_orderable'.\n\nThis suggests that korma should be on the 'orderable' list. Now we need to make sure everyone who dislikes korma is still satisfied:\n\n- Yue dislikes korma and likes tiramisu, macaron (which are contentious).\n- Kim dislikes korma and dislikes gelato, macaron (making macaron a good candidate for 'not_orderable').\n- Gen dislikes korma and dislikes tiramisu (which we can't put on 'orderable').\n- Riya dislikes korma, gelato, and tiramisu. (This is problematic since all items Riya dislikes are also liked by others.)\n\nGiven that Riya's preferences conflict with those of the others, we don't have a clear candidate for 'not_orderable' among the options disliked by Riya. We're now facing a contradiction: an item left off the 'orderable' list to satisfy one person's dislikes would need to be included to satisfy another's likes. \n\nFor instance, to satisfy Riya, we need to not order gelato, tiramisu, or korma, but at least one of these needs to be ordered to satisfy the likes of other individuals.\n\nUpon this realization, we must conclude that it is impossible to satisfy all participants with any combination of 'orderable' and 'not_orderable'. Thus, the output for both will be empty lists:\n\n```python\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 918, 'num_completion_tokens': 731}
