gh this step-by-step.\n\n1. **Identify any conflicts**: First, we should identify any items that are liked by some individuals and disliked by others. These items will be trickier to place in our lists because they cannot satisfy both parties at the same time.\n\nHere are the conflicts:\n\n- **Salad**: Liked by Diya, Fay, Ula, Kai, Jay, Raj, and Ray, but disliked by Zara and Lan.\n- **Shawarma**: Liked by Diya, Mel, Fay, Jay, Sue, Tao, but disliked by Chen, Chao, and Kavi.\n- **Tart**: Liked by Ying, Mina, Kai, Nita, but disliked by Diya, Lin, Eva.\n- **Burger**: Liked by Zara, Ty, Lia, Nita, Ray, but disliked by Zara, Cal, Kai, Sam and Qi. \n- **Guacamole**: Liked by Liz, Mel, Fay, Eva, Chen, Sue, Nita, but disliked by Mel, Lan, Ru, Ula, Lia, Qi.\n- **Baklava**: Liked by Liz, Cal, Eva, Ula, Chen, Sue, Chao, Qi, but disliked by Liz, Ty, Lia, Sam.\n- **Sushi**: Liked by Lan, Sam, Raj, but disliked by Lin, Kavi, Jay.\n- **Brownies**: Liked by Liz, Ying, Kavi, Chao, Ray, but disliked by Mel, Ru, Qi.\n- **Paneer**: Liked by Zara, Ty, Ru, but disliked by Lin, Cal, Raj.\n\n2. **Create preliminary lists**: Next, let's try to create preliminary lists that satisfy as many individuals as possible. We should start with items that have unanimous opinions (liked by some but not disliked by any or the opposite).\n\n3. **Refine the lists**: We will have to refine these lists to make sure all individuals are satisfied, paying attention to the conflicts identified.\n\nLet's start putting together what we can:\n\nFirstly, we should find items that are disliked by at least one person and not liked by anyone else. We can safely place these in 'not_orderable' since they won't conflict with anyone's likes. We can't locate such items in this case because every disliked item is also liked by someone else.\n\nWith no clear items that we can place in 'not_orderable' right away, we now look for items that are liked by at least one person and not disliked by anyone else to place in 'orderable'