t's start with the 'dislikes' because they are more critical in ensuring that no one gets a food item they dislike:\n\n- Falafel is disliked by almost everyone except Rob, Wei, Lex, Mina, and Zan, none of whom dislikes all orderable items. So, we can put falafel in 'not_orderable'.\n- Waffles are disliked by a few (Bea, Jay, Ty, Bao, Rob, Tia, Ray, Jaya, and Joy), but many people who dislike waffles like something else, except for Tia and Ray, who dislike all three items. This creates an issue because we cannot simultaneously satisfy these individuals by placing waffles in either 'orderable' or 'not_orderable'.\n- Fries are disliked by Eli, Kit, Bao, Tia, and Pat. Everyone who dislikes fries has another option, except Tia.\n- Toast is disliked by Tao, Xan, Ivy, Lei, Kim, Ray, Wei, and Zan. Since Ray already has an issue with waffles, it's impossible to satisfy everyone regardless of the placement of toast.\n\nAt this point, it's clear that we can't satisfy Tia and Ray because they dislike all items, and there are people who only like the items Tia and Ray dislike. Hence, it's impossible to create a list satisfying everyone's food preferences.\n\nTherefore, our final solution lists will be empty:\n\n```\norderable=[], not_orderable=[]\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 512, 'num_completion_tokens': 424}
