d and disliked by at least one person, so no item can be immediately placed into a list solely based on this criterion.\n\nLet's analyze the items based on who likes and dislikes them. We'll try to identify items that can satisfy as many people as possible when placed in `orderable` and `not_orderable`.\n\nAnalysing item by item:\n\n1. **Frittata**:\n- Several people like it: Lin, Cal, Qi, Neil, Anil, Sia, Sue, Wes, Ben, Wei, Joy.\n- Many people dislike it: Vic, Arun, Ula, Bea, Nita, Hui, Chen, Xan, Pia, Max, Eli, Isha, Mina, Amy.\nBecause more people dislike frittata (14) than those who like it (11), it might be sensible to consider putting frittata in `not_orderable`.\n\n2. **Tiramisu**:\n- Many people like it: Lin, Ula, Lan, Lex, Naina, Lee, Ty, Pam, Lex, Naina, Lee, Sue, Ava, Joy.\n- Several people dislike it: Gus, Zan, Zac, Jun, Eli, Wei, Bo.\nIn this case, more people like tiramisu (14) than dislike it (7), suggesting it might be a good candidate for `orderable`.\n\n3. **Churros**:\n- Liked by: Lin, Zoe, Bea, Nita, Cal, Chen, Pam, Ru, Rina, Bao, Riya, Bo.\n- Disliked by: Vic, Gus, Ian, Jun, Qi, Eli, Wei, Joy, Zan, Isha, Mina.\nThe preference for churros is split fairly evenly, so it isn't a straightforward candidate for either list yet without considering other items.\n\n4. **Guacamole**:\n- Liked by: Bea, Ian, Hui, Jun, Max, Raj, Sia, Anil, Isha, Mina, Bo.\n- Disliked by: Vic, Arun, Ula, Taj, Pia, Lee, Lex, Naina, Ava, Ben, Ty.\nGuacamole is liked slightly more than it is disliked (11 versus 10), which makes it a difficult choice without further analysis.\n\n5. **Espresso**:\n- Liked by: Arun, Zoe, Nita, Zac, Lou, Anil, Amy, Ava, Ty, Joy.\n- Disliked by: Vic, Gus, Ian, Taj, Chen, Lan, Lex, Lee, Ben, Wei, Rina, Ru, Eli.\nGiven that espresso is disliked by more people (13) than who like it (10), it could reasonably go into `not_orderable`.\n\n6. **Nachos**:\n- Liked by: Zoe, Taj, May, Pia, Max, Pam, Raj, Sia, Tom, Ava, Sue.\n- Disliked by: Gus, Zan, Hui, Neil, 