er, Val, Bao dislike it but have other items (cheese, tandoori, pizza) they can be satisfied with.\n- Tiramisu goes to 'orderable' because it's necessary for Xan, Ken, Gus, Ned, Nita, Qi, and many others like it. However, Hu, Veer, Jan, Kai, Mei, Nita have other dislikes they can be satisfied with.\n- Pizza should be 'orderable' as it satisfies Dot, Zan, Tim, Mina, Naina, Cal, Isha, Yan, Lou, Om, Pam, Ansh, Geet. Hu, Jon, Bo, Zan have other dislikes.\n- Cheese goes to 'orderable' to satisfy Pat, Rex, Veer, Val, Gen, Sol, Bao, Mia. Lin can be satisfied with 'not_orderable' items.\n- Couscous can be 'not_orderable' without much issue as only Lee, Li, Cy, Pam, Ned prefer it, and they have other likes.\n\n**The Orderable list:**\n- Caramel\n- Tiramisu\n- Pizza\n- Cheese\n\n**The Not_Orderable list:**\n- Couscous\n\nGiven these selections, everyone is satisfied either by having a like in 'orderable' or a dislike in 'not_orderable'.\n\nFinally, we can output the result:\n\n```python\norderable=['caramel', 'tiramisu', 'pizza', 'cheese']\nnot_orderable=['couscous']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 776, 'num_completion_tokens': 1216}
