\n- falafel: Kai, Min, Wei, Ron, Mel\n- espresso: Naina, Shan, Min, Xiu, Ivy, Liz, Om\n- shawarma: Yue, Naina, Ada, Sky, Ava, Ron\n- vindaloo: Jan, Pia, Ivy, Om\n- gelato: Jan, Liv, Jim, Ron, Sky\n- salmon: Qi, Ron, Om\n- tiramisu: Pia, Tara, Sky, Ron\n\nOrderable and not_orderable list strategy:\n\n1. Make a list of items that no one likes but at least one person dislikes. These can directly go into the 'not_orderable' list.\n2. Make a list of items that at least one person likes and no one dislikes. These can directly go into the 'orderable' list.\n3. For the remaining items, where both liking and disliking are present, we need to balance the likes and dislikes to satisfy everyone.\n\nFrom the dislikes list, we see:\n- Espresso is disliked by the most number of people (7 individuals: Naina, Shan, Min, Xiu, Ivy, Liz, Om) and it is liked by four (Yue, Ned, Om, Abe). It could be a candidate for the ‘not_orderable’ list depending on Abe's and Ned's other likes.\n- Vindaloo is disliked by 4 people (Jan, Pia, Ivy, Om) and liked by 5 (Kai, Naina, Jim, Liz, Ned). We need to see if it could satisfy some people if placed in either list.\n- Tiramusu is disliked by 4 people (Pia, Tara, Sky, Ron), but liked by 2 (Mel, Sid). We may put this in ‘not_orderable’ if Mel and Sid have other likes.\n\nLooking at the likes list:\n- Toast is liked by 4 individuals (Yue, Qi, Ava, Liz) and disliked by 4 (Kai, Ada, Pia, Ivy), making it a challenging item to place.\n- Gelato is liked by 5 (Shan, Wei, Tara, Sky, Abe), but disliked also by 5 (Jan, Liv, Jim, Ron, Sky). This will need careful consideration since Sky likes and dislikes it (which must be a mistake), so we can safely assume gelato is only disliked by 4.\n- Shawarma is liked by 6 (Shan, Jan, Xiu, Liv, Ava, Mel), disliked by 3 (Yue, Naina, Ada), which isn't straightforward to place.\n\nWith the conflict items in mind, let's list what we can determine directly:\n\nDirect not_orderable:\n- tiramisu (disliked by Pia, Tara, Sky, Ron and only liked by Mel, Sid who have other likes)\n\nDirect orderable: (There are none without conflict)\n\nWe now need to work through the conflict items to see if we can satisfy everyone's likes while avoiding their dislikes:\n\n1. Espresso has more dislikes than likes and no one who likes espresso dislikes all the other items they like since Abe likes salmon and gelato, Om likes vindaloo as well, and Ned likes falafel and vindaloo. So espresso should go to ‘not_orderable’.\n   \n2. Looking at vindaloo, we have 5 likes and 4 dislikes. We can include vindaloo in ‘orderable’ since no one who dislikes vindaloo dislikes all of their likes as well.\n   \n3. Toast is tricky but necessary for Yue, Qi, Ava, and Liz to be satisfied. None of them has a second liked item that they could all agree on, and Kai, Ada, and Ivy who dislike toast can be satisfied by espresso and tiramisu being ‘not_orderable’. So toast should be ‘orderable’.\n   \n4. Shawarma has more likes than dislikes, but we need to check if the people who dislike it can be satisfied otherwise. Yue is satisfied with toast, Naina with vindaloo, and Ada with falafel in ‘orderable’. So, shawarma can be ‘orderable’.\n\n5. Gelato has equal support and dislike, but all those disliking gelato have another item they dislike which is not orderable, so we can place gelato in ‘orderable’.\n   \n6. Salmon only has three individuals disliking it (Qi, Ron, Om), and they can be satisfied with other items in the ‘not_orderable’ list (Qi with espresso, Ron and Om with tiramisu), so salmon can be ‘orderable’.\n\nFalafel can be placed in the ‘orderable’ as Tara who likes falafel is satisfied with gelato being orderable and all people who disliked falafel are already satisfied with the other items in the ‘not_orderable’ list.\n\nThis results in the following lists:\n\norderable = ['toast', 'shawarma', 'vindaloo', 'gelato', 'salmon', 'falafel']\nnot_orderable = ['espresso', 'tiramisu']\n\noutputting this in python code format:\n\norderable=['toast', 'shawarma', 'vindaloo', 'gelato', 'salmon', 'falafel'], not_orderable=['espresso', 'tiramisu']", 'num_prompt_tokens': 534, 'num_completion_tokens': 1250}
