i: Likes pho, ratatouille. Dislikes cheesecake. Wei: Likes brownies, wonton. Dislikes shrimps. Arun: Likes shrimps, brownies, pho. Tim: Likes ratatouille. Dislikes shrimps, pho. Tia: Likes tandoori. Dislikes cheesecake, pho. Ned: Dislikes wonton, brownies, bruschetta. Mina: Likes shrimps. Dislikes ratatouille, tandoori. Wes: Likes brownies, shrimps, ratatouille. Lin: Likes bruschetta. Dislikes shrimps, ratatouille. Ray: Likes shrimps, ratatouille. Dislikes cheesecake. Ying: Likes brownies. Dislikes tandoori, cheesecake. Lex: Likes tandoori, brownies. Dislikes ratatouille. Bao: Likes brownies. Dislikes tandoori, wonton. Shan: Likes shrimps, pho, bruschetta. Kim: Likes wonton, brownies. Dislikes bruschetta. Mel: Likes tandoori, brownies. Dislikes bruschetta. Rex: Likes pho, cheesecake. Dislikes wonton. Ty: Likes shrimps. Dislikes pho, bruschetta. Kavi: Likes ratatouille, brownies. Dislikes shrimps. Tao: Likes brownies. Dislikes ratatouille, bruschetta. Feng: Likes brownies, ratatouille. Dislikes cheesecake. Qi: Likes brownies. Dislikes pho, cheesecake. Zara: Likes pho. Dislikes ratatouille, bruschetta. Ana: Likes shrimps. Dislikes bruschetta, ratatouille. Ben: Likes wonton. Dislikes ratatouille, bruschetta. Zoe: Likes ratatouille, pho. Dislikes wonton. Eli: Likes ratatouille. Dislikes cheesecake, shrimps. Ada: Likes shrimps. Dislikes brownies, ratatouille. Fay: Likes tandoori, ratatouille, pho. Jun: Likes brownies, pho. Dislikes wonton. Amy: Likes shrimps, tandoori. Dislikes wonton. Pam: Likes tandoori, wonton. Dislikes shrimps. Meg: Likes shrimps, ratatouille. Dislikes bruschetta. Nita: Likes ratatouille. Dislikes brownies, tandoori. Raj: Likes shrimps, ratatouille. Dislikes pho. Geet: Dislikes shrimps, pho, bruschetta. Pia: Likes bruschetta. Dislikes brownies, wonton. Bo: Likes shrimps, cheesecake. Dislikes brownies. Diya: Likes cheesecake, tandoori. Dislikes shrimps. Abe: Likes tandoori, brownies, cheesecake. Hu: Dislikes ratatouille, wonton, bruschetta. Sam: Likes wonton. Dislikes bruschetta, pho. Joy: Dislikes shrimps, brownies, ratatouille. Lei: Likes pho, bruschetta, shrimps. Li: Likes shrimps. Dislikes ratatouille, tandoori. Joe: Likes tandoori. Dislikes bruschetta, brownies. Zac: Likes wonton, cheesecake. Dislikes bruschetta. Dan: Likes bruschetta, ratatouille. Dislikes pho. Jan: Likes wonton. Dislikes bruschetta, brownies. Bea: Likes wonton, bruschetta, tandoori. Yan: Likes pho. Dislikes brownies, ratatouille. Aarav: Dislikes bruschetta, brownies, pho. Zan: Likes tandoori, cheesecake. Dislikes wonton. Jim: Likes brownies, bruschetta. Dislikes ratatouille. Ken: Likes cheesecake, brownies. Dislikes shrimps. Gia: Likes brownies. Dislikes wonton, bruschetta. Rob: Dislikes shrimps, cheesecake, wonton. Tom: Likes cheesecake. Dislikes tandoori, bruschetta. Lou: Likes shrimps. Dislikes pho, tandoori. Cy: Likes wonton, brownies. Dislikes cheesecake. Ravi: Likes pho. Dislikes wonton, cheesecake. Du: Likes cheesecake, shrimps. Dislikes bruschetta. Gen: Dislikes tandoori, pho, bruschetta. Jon: Likes wonton. Dislikes shrimps, tandoori. May: Likes cheesecake, bruschetta. Dislikes shrimps. Sal: Likes shrimps, ratatouille. Dislikes bruschetta. Ansh: Likes pho, tandoori. Dislikes shrimps. Sue: Likes ratatouille. Dislikes tandoori, cheesecake. Kit: Likes tandoori, bruschetta. Dislikes pho. Xiu: Dislikes bruschetta, cheesecake, brownies. Lan: Likes brownies. Dislikes shrimps, bruschetta. Dot: Likes bruschetta. Dislikes wonton, shrimps. ', 'menu_items': ['cheesecake', 'shrimps', 'brownies', 'bruschetta', 'wonton', 'pho', 'tandoori', 'ratatouille'], 'gpt_out': 'To satisfy the criteria given, we need to identify items that can satisfy the maximum number of individuals when ordered and the ones to avoid so as to not dissatisfy others.\n\nFirst, let\'s identify the items that are liked or disliked by the individuals.\n\nItems that are liked (along with the number of people who like them)\n\n- ratatouille: 14\n- tandoori: 11\n- cheesecake: 14\n- bruschetta: 6\n- shrimps: 18\n- wonton: 9\n- pho: 12\n- brownies: 15\n\nItems that are disliked (along with the number of people who dislike them)\n\n- pho: 16\n- brownies: 14\n- bruschetta: 24\n- shrimps: 15\n- cheesecake: 10\n- ratatouille: 14\n- tandoori: 12\n- wonton: 11\n\nNext, we will attempt to place items into \'orderable\' and \'not_orderable\' lists such that everyone is satisfied according to the criteria mentioned. However, we see that certain items are liked by some people and disliked by others, making it challenging to satisfy everyone\'s preferences.\n\nNow, let\'s look at the disliked items first as they will reduce the possible combinations:\n\n- Bruschetta is disliked the most (24 people), followed by pho, shrimps, brownies, and tandoori.\n\nSince bruschetta is the most disliked, we will start by placing it in the \'not_orderable\' list as that decision will satisfy the preferences of 24 individuals. Next, the item liked by the most number of individuals not already satisfied is shrimps. Since shrimps are also disliked by individuals (and we can\'t make them simultaneously \'orderable\' and \'not_orderable\'), we will exclude shrimps from \'orderable\' and place them in \'not_orderable\'. \n\nNext, we add ratatouille to \'orderable\' since it is the next most liked item by those who are not already satisfied by the \'not_orderable\' list. Following this, no other food can be added to the \'orderable\' list without making at least one person dissatisfied.\n\nNow we have:\n\nOrderable: ratatouille\nNot_orderable: bruschetta, shrimps\n\nThere may be individuals who haven\'t been satisfied yet, but we cannot satisfy everyone given the constraints, as many individuals dislike what others like. The cross-matching of likes and dislikes creates a scenario where no perfect solution satisfies all the conditions. Therefore, the problem doesn\'t have a completely satisfactory solution for all individuals based on the given criteria. \n\nSo, the final solution, which satisfies as many individuals as possible without violating the constraints is:\n\n```python\norderable=["ratatouille"], not_orderable=["bruschetta", "shrimps"]\n``` \n\nThis list attempts to minimize dissatisfaction while understanding that not all participants can be satisfied.', 'num_prompt_tokens': 1601, 'num_completion_tokens': 625}
