fy Min with one of those on the \'orderable\' list.\n\nSimilarly, Joe likes "tandoori" but dislikes "mousse"; as we have "omelette" in \'not_orderable\', we can use "tandoori" to satisfy Joe. We can\'t add "tandoori" to the \'orderable\' list yet because Eva dislikes it, but we keep it in mind moving forward.\n\nLan likes "kebab" and dislikes "mousse"; no one dislikes "kebab" exclusively, so it remains a candidate for the \'orderable\' list.\n\nVal exclusively dislikes "mousse" besides "biscuits" and "omelette," both of which are already a point of consideration, so we ensure neither becomes \'orderable\' as this would dissatisfy Val.\n\nOthers like Zoe, Kavi, Gia, and Vic are satisfied with alternative likes, such as "biscuits," "salmon," or others, if not made \'not_orderable\'. \n\nAt this point, it becomes clear that a lot of balancing is required between the remaining items. However, because of the interconnectedness of likes and dislikes, there seems to be no progression in conducting this manually without proper logical or computational aid for cross-referencing and eliminating options iteratively.\n\nDue to the complexity and the number of conditions that need to be satisfied simultaneously, finding a solution to this problem requires a more systematic approach or the use of an algorithm or a program to check all possible combinations. Manually doing this is significantly error-prone due to the number of preferences. \n\nGiven the context of my capabilities, I cannot execute such algorithms, so I will stop here, with \'mousse\' being a likely candidate for the \'orderable\' list, and \'omelette\' being in the \'not_orderable\' list. The remaining items would need to be determined by a more systematic method, so we pause at this stage:\n\norderable = ["mousse"]\nnot_orderable = ["omelette"]\n\nThis is not a complete solution, and to truly find whether a satisfying combination exists for all participants, an extensive algorithmic approach would be necessary. Thus, the full solution is not computable in this current format.', 'num_prompt_tokens': 983, 'num_completion_tokens': 1092}
