d items that can be placed in the 'orderable' list. Since 'korma' is only moderately disliked and liked by several participants who have no other liked items in the 'orderable' list yet, we should include 'korma' in 'orderable'. Moreover, 'korma' is the only liked food item for Xan who dislikes 'sorbet' and 'ramen,' so it needs to be in 'orderable'.\n\nGiven these considerations, the 'orderable' and 'not_orderable' lists could be as follows:\n\n- orderable: korma\n- not_orderable: macaron\n\nNow we must check if these lists satisfy all individuals' preferences:\n\n- Korma satisfies Vic, Ula, Xan, and Pat. (since it's their liked item)\n- Korma does not satisfy Nic (since he dislikes it) unless burger and/or ramen is also in 'orderable' (and it can be, as his other dislikes are not required for anyone else’s satisfaction).\n- Macaron in 'not_orderable' satisfies Nita, Amy, Hui, Isha, Sam, Min, and Rohan. (since it's their disliked item)\n- Macaron in 'not_orderable' does not satisfy Jay unless one of his likes, burger or shrimps, is made 'orderable', which can be done since they are not disliked by someone who needs those dislikes for satisfaction.\n- Macaron in 'not_orderable' does not satisfy Abe unless one of his likes, burger or pie, is made 'orderable', which we can do.\n\n\nContinuing on checking and adjusting:\n\n- For all individuals who disliked macaron and do not have a like in the 'orderable' list yet, we will need to add one of their likes to 'orderable'.\n- We will add 'burger' to 'orderable' to satisfy Jay and Abe as well as Nic who dislikes korma. \n\nNow we update our lists:\n\n- orderable: [korma, burger]\n- not_orderable: [macaron]\n\nFinal check:\n\n- With 'burger' now in 'orderable', Gen is also satisfied.\n- No one is only left with 'wonton' as a like, so it is safe to include 'wonton' in 'not_orderable'.\n\nFinal lists after update:\n\n- orderable: [korma, burger]\n- not_orderable: [macaron, wonton]\n\nFinal check for satisfaction:\n\n- Everyone