Data Sample: {'num_vars': 5, 'num_clauses': 20, 'formula': [[1, -3, 2], [1, -3, 4], [-1, -3, -2], [3, -2, -1], [-2, -3, -5], [-5, 2, 1], [-3, -1, 5], [1, -3, -4], [5, 2, -4], [1, -3, 2], [-1, -3, 4], [-2, 1, -4], [-4, -3, 2], [-5, -3, -1], [-2, 1, 5], [-2, -3, -1], [3, 1, 2], [-4, 2, 3], [-5, 4, -2], [-5, 2, -3]], 'is_sat': True, 'preferences': 'Max: Likes naan, caramel. Dislikes gelato. Amy: Likes naan, cheesecake. Dislikes gelato. Ty: Dislikes naan, gelato, caramel. Pia: Likes gelato. Dislikes caramel, naan. Om: Dislikes caramel, gelato, risotto. Ana: Likes caramel, naan. Dislikes risotto. Arun: Likes risotto. Dislikes gelato, naan. Sam: Likes naan. Dislikes gelato, cheesecake. Sue: Likes risotto, caramel. Dislikes cheesecake. Ian: Likes naan, caramel. Dislikes gelato. Tara: Likes cheesecake. Dislikes naan, gelato. Zac: Likes naan. Dislikes caramel, cheesecake. Riya: Likes caramel. Dislikes cheesecake, gelato. Rohan: Dislikes risotto, gelato, naan. Gia: Likes naan, risotto. Dislikes caramel. Lia: Dislikes caramel, gelato, naan. Mel: Likes gelato, naan, caramel. Mia: Likes caramel, gelato. Dislikes cheesecake. Hal: Likes cheesecake. Dislikes risotto, caramel. Bao: Likes caramel. Dislikes risotto, gelato. ', 'menu_items': ['naan', 'caramel', 'gelato', 'cheesecake', 'risotto'], 'gpt_out': "To satisfy everyone, we need to find at least one item that each person likes in the 'orderable' list or one item they dislike in the 'not_orderable' list. Let’s analyze the preferences to find a common ground for the 'orderable' and 'not_orderable' lists:\n\n1. **Gelato:** is disliked by many. Pia, Mel, and Mia like gelato. However, it is noted that Mel and Mia also like caramel, which means that if gelato is in 'not_orderable', they can still be satisfied with caramel. Pia is the only one with a unique preference for gelato.\n\n2. **Naan:** is liked by many and disliked by a significant number as well. It seems to be a common liked item, but placing it in either list would dissatisfy a group.\n\n3. **Caramel:** is liked by many and only disliked by a few.\n\n4. **Risotto:** Multiples like it, multiple dislikes.\n\n5. **Cheesecake:** Several people like it, and several dislike it.\n\nNow let’s attempt to construct our lists:\n\n- **not_orderable:** Could have gelato since Pia can be satisfied by an absence of her disliked items, namely caramel and naan; and others who like gelato also like other items that could potentially be ordered.\n\n- **orderable:** We can consider caramel for the 'orderable' list since it is liked by many and disliked only by a few (those who dislike caramel either have other likes or dislikes that can be used to satisfy their preferences).\n\nNow we'll try filling our lists while ensuring all participants are satisfied:\n\n1. Place gelato in 'not_orderable' because fewer people dislike not having it (particularly Pia, who could be satisfied with the absence of caramel and naan).\n2. Add caramel to 'orderable' because most who like it only dislike gelato, which will be in 'not_orderable'.\n3. We cannot add naan to 'orderable' because Ty, Lia, and Rohan dislike it. Likewise, we cannot add it to 'not_orderable' because many who like naan don't have an alternative like.\n4. We cannot add cheesecake to either list for the same reason as naan; it is liked and disliked by too many.\n5. Risotto is the same as naan and cheesecake; adding it to either list would dissatisfy other individuals.\n\nLet's check if everyone can be satisfied with these lists:\n\n- Max: Satisfied with caramel.\n- Amy: Satisfied with caramel.\n- Ty: Satisfied with gelato in 'not_orderable'.\n- Pia: Satisfied with gelato in 'not_orderable'.\n- Om: Satisfied with caramel and gelato in 'not_orderable'.\n- Ana: Satisfied with caramel.\n- Arun: Satisfied with gelato in 'not_orderable'.\n- Sam: Satisfied with caramel.\n- Sue: Satisfied with caramel.\n- Ian: Satisfied with caramel.\n- Tara: Satisfied with gelato in 'not_orderable' and caramel not in 'not_orderable'.\n- Zac: Satisfied with caramel.\n- Riya: Satisfied with caramel.\n- Rohan: Satisfied with gelato in 'not_orderable'.\n- Gia: Satisfied with caramel as there is no naan in 'orderable'.\n- Lia: Satisfied with gelato in 'not_orderable'.\n- Mel: Satisfied with caramel.\n- Mia: Satisfied with caramel.\n- Hal: Not satisfied yet, but we can fix this by adding cheesecake to 'orderable', since the people who dislike cheesecake (Sam, Zac, Riya) are already satisfied with caramel.\n- Bao: Satisfied with caramel.\n\nEveryone can be satisfied with gelato in 'not_orderable', caramel in 'orderable', and we'll add cheesecake to 'orderable' to satisfy Hal, considering Sam, Zac, and Riya can still be satisfied by caramel. The final solution is:\n\n```python\norderable=['caramel', 'cheesecake'], not_orderable=['gelato']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 457, 'num_completion_tokens': 855}
Data Sample: {'num_vars': 9, 'num_clauses': 63, 'formula': [[-8, -5, 6], [5, -1, -2], [-5, 7, 8], [5, 3, 6], [8, -1, 3], [3, 2, -1], [-2, -8, 7], [-3, 5, -4], [-7, -5, 3], [-4, -7, 1], [-1, -3, 7], [-1, -2, 4], [-3, -1, 7], [-9, 2, -7], [7, 1, -3], [-1, -7, 2], [-4, -3, 7], [-1, 3, -5], [1, -6, -7], [2, 7, 1], [1, -9, -7], [5, 9, -4], [1, -2, 4], [4, 7, 5], [-5, 8, -1], [3, -1, -8], [-6, -8, 9], [-3, -6, 8], [9, 4, 8], [7, 9, -1], [2, 9, 5], [6, 7, -9], [-2, 9, 7], [-7, 3, 5], [-6, -1, 4], [4, -5, -9], [4, -3, 7], [5, 6, 8], [-5, 2, -1], [-8, 4, -6], [6, 5, -8], [-1, -2, 4], [-3, 8, -7], [-6, 7, -8], [-9, 1, -8], [2, -5, -4], [8, 6, 5], [-5, 3, -2], [-4, -7, 6], [-7, 2, -5], [4, 2, -8], [-4, -6, 8], [-4, 5, -1], [-2, -9, 6], [1, -7, 4], [1, 7, -3], [-2, -7, -3], [3, 6, 1], [-1, 4, -3], [3, 6, 1], [3, -4, 9], [8, 1, 4], [1, -6, 3]], 'is_sat': False, 'preferences': 'Ian: Likes ravioli. Dislikes peach, paneer. Meg: Likes paneer. Dislikes doughnut, lobster. Rina: Likes salmon, peach. Dislikes paneer. Mia: Likes paneer, wonton, ravioli. Joy: Likes peach, wonton. Dislikes doughnut. Ula: Likes wonton, lobster. Dislikes doughnut. Nic: Likes salmon. Dislikes lobster, peach. Fay: Likes paneer. Dislikes wonton, guacamole. Ty: Likes wonton. Dislikes salmon, paneer. Ben: Likes doughnut. Dislikes guacamole, salmon. Pam: Likes salmon. Dislikes doughnut, wonton. Qi: Likes guacamole. Dislikes doughnut, lobster. Mei: Likes salmon. Dislikes wonton, doughnut. Tom: Likes lobster. Dislikes naan, salmon. Mina: Likes salmon, doughnut. Dislikes wonton. Ned: Likes lobster. Dislikes doughnut, salmon. Sam: Likes salmon. Dislikes guacamole, wonton. Geet: Likes wonton. Dislikes doughnut, paneer. Zara: Likes doughnut. Dislikes ravioli, salmon. Sid: Likes lobster, salmon, doughnut. Max: Likes doughnut. Dislikes naan, salmon. Zac: Likes paneer, naan. Dislikes guacamole. Pat: Likes doughnut, guacamole. Dislikes lobster. Jaya: Likes guacamole, salmon, paneer. Yue: Likes peach. Dislikes paneer, doughn