'not_orderable'. \n\nThus, we can consider the following:\n- not_orderable: Cake\n- orderable: Wonton\n\nNow let's try to satisfy those who liked or disliked Ramen. Om likes Ramen and dislikes Guacamole and Espresso. Since Espresso is not universally disliked and is liked by some, we cannot place it on the 'not_orderable' list. Guacamole is liked by many, so it cannot go on the 'not_orderable' list either. However, no one who dislikes Ramen likes it (Jim, Leo, Fay, Sue, Zac, May), so we can add Ramen to the 'orderable' list to satisfy Om and others who have not been satisfied yet will not be affected:\n\n- orderable: Wonton, Ramen\n\nNext, Omelette is liked by several and disliked by many who are already satisfied by Cake being 'not_orderable' – except for Sue, who still wouldn't be satisfied as she dislikes both Guacamole and Ramen. To keep Omelette 'orderable', we would need to place Guacamole in the 'not_orderable' list, which is highly liked. However, Ike and Rina who like Omelette, dislike Guacamole. To satisfy them, we can keep Omelette in 'orderable':\n\n- orderable: Wonton, Ramen, Omelette\n\nSue still needs to be satisfied. Looking at what Sue dislikes (Ramen, Guacamole, Omelette), it's difficult to satisfy her since her dislikes are already in the orderable list or too liked to be in the 'not_orderable' list. Let's put Guacamole in ‘not_orderable’, which will satisfy Sue as well as Xiu, Rina, Om, Lei, and many others who dislike it:\n\n- not_orderable: Cake, Guacamole\n\nBy placing Guacamole in 'not_orderable', we need to ensure Eli, Hu, Qi, Tia, Zac are all satisfied since they like Guacamole. Pancakes are not disliked by anyone who dislikes Guacamole, except by Ron, who is already satisfied by having Cake in the 'not_orderable' list, and others who dislike Guacamole don't have Pancakes on their liked list. So we can add Pancakes to 'orderable':\n\n- orderable: Wonton, Ramen, Omelette, Pancakes\n\nNow, most individuals should be satisfied, except for those who dislike Falafel and we need to ensure that Espresso is also added to the ‘orderable’ list to satisfy people who like it and are not yet satisfied (Rohan and Lei, for instance):\n\n- orderable: Wonton, Ramen, Omelette, Pancakes, Espresso\n\nSince no one else has exclusively liked Falafel without liking something already in the ‘orderable’ list or disliked something in the 'not_orderable' list, and considering the remaining preferences:\n\n- Those who like Falafel (Leo, Fay, Geet) can be satisfied with Ramen, Pancakes, or Omelette which are in the 'orderable' list.\n- Those who dislike Falafel (Jim, Ian) are already satisfied with Ramen in the 'orderable' list or Cake and Guacamole in the 'not_orderable' list.\n\nNow, let's list who is satisfied by likes and dislikes:\n\nSatisfied by 'orderable' likes:\n- Xiu: Wonton\n- Max: Omelette, Pancakes\n- Ty: Ramen, Espresso\n- Jim: Cheese (needs to be orderable)\n- Wes: Cheese (needs to be orderable)\n- Hu: Wonton, Pancakes\n- Eli: Wonton, Omelette\n- Raj: Espresso, Omelette\n- Rina: Omelette\n- Rohan: Cheese (needs to be orderable), Espresso\n- Ping: Cheese (needs to be orderable), Espresso, Omelette\n- Om: Ramen\n- Lei: Espresso\n- Zac: Satisfied by Guacamole in 'not_orderable'\n\nSatisfied by 'not_orderable' dislikes:\n- Sol: Cake\n- Ian: Cake\n- Lin: Cake\n- Ron: Cake\n- May: Satisfied by Ramen in 'orderable'\n- Sue: Guacamole\n\nSatisfied by other criteria:\n- Leo: Falafel in orderable\n- Qi: Pancakes in orderable\n- Tia: Satisfied by Guacamole in 'not_orderable'\n- Abe: Wonton in orderable\n- Ben: Espresso in orderable\n- Geet: Omelette in orderable\n- Fay: Falafel in orderable\n\nSince Cheese is liked by Jim, Wes, Rohan, and Ping and not exclusively disliked by anyone satisfied by something else already, we will add Cheese to 'orderable':\n\n- orderable: Wonton, Ramen, Omelette, Pancakes, Espresso, Cheese\n\nFinally, let's review satisfaction as we have now incorporated an item Jim and Wes like into 'orderable':\