n be satisfied with ravioli in 'orderable' and shawarma not, since she dislikes roti. \n\nBy following this process, the final 'orderable' foods are korma, ravioli, and roti, and the 'not_orderable' foods are risotto, poke, spaghetti, and shawarma. Every individual has at least one like in 'orderable' or one dislike in 'not_orderable', thus all are satisfied.\n\nHere is the final solution:\n\n```python\norderable=['korma', 'ravioli', 'roti'], not_orderable=['risotto', 'poke', 'spaghetti', 'shawarma']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 392, 'num_completion_tokens': 960}
