n, Hal, conflict if not included)\n\nBased on dislikes these cannot be on orderable list:\n- hummus (disliked by Abe, Bo, Bea, strong pressure to exclude)\n- cheese (disliked by Ansh, Ula, Yue, would generate conflict if included)\n- couscous (disliked by Ana, Ron, Lei, conflict if included)\n- quiche (disliked by Qi and Lia, pressure to exclude)\n- peach (major dislikes from Isha, Qi, Lia)\n\nLet's try to put these on the 'not_orderable' list and see if we can satisfy everyone's preferences:\n\nStep 2: Populate the 'not_orderable' List:\n- hummus\n- cheese\n- couscous\n- quiche\n- peach\n\nThe 'not_orderable' list satisfies Qi and Ana as they both dislike items that appear here (Qi dislikes peach and quiche, Ana dislikes couscous).\n\nNow we need to determine the 'orderable' list using the likes of the remaining unsatisfied individuals.\n\nOnto the 'orderable' list:\n- falafel (satisfies Kit, Ansh, Rohan, Lei, Eli, Bea, Ron)\n- caramel (satisfies Kit, Ivy, Yue)\n- tacos (satisfies Kit, Ying, Sue, Rohan, Ben)\n- sushi (satisfies Kavi, Ana, Jon, Hal)\n\nStep 3: Validate That All Are Satisfied:\n\nBefore finalizing these lists, a careful check is needed to ensure all individuals have at least one liked or disliked item on the correct list:\n\nUnsatisfied with these lists and their preference satisfaction requirement includes:\n- Bo (none of the items Bo likes are on orderable, and dislikes (caramel, hummus) are not both on the not_orderable list)\n- Kavi (dislikes are not an issue, but cheese being on the not_orderable list makes it impossible to satisfy Kavi without breaking other rules)\n- Yan (sushi is orderable, but cheese is not, thus Yan can be satisfied)\n- Ula (cheese is not on the orderable list, which makes it impossible for Ula to be satisfied)\n\nIt looks like we cannot satisfy all participants with this configuration.\n\nGiven the complex interplay of likes and dislikes, it becomes nearly impossible to create a combination that satisfies all individuals. 