 Gen, Lan, Sue, Hui, Max (5 likes). Disliked by Jay, Wes, Rex, Ru (4 dislikes).\n3. Cheese: Liked by Gen, Wes, Li, Ty, Hui, Sky, Sue (7 likes). Disliked by Lin, Anil, Wei, Rohan (4 dislikes).\n4. Cheesecake: Liked by Ana, Li, Chao, Xiu, Ansh (5 likes). Disliked by Lin, Jay, Hui, Ty, Wei, Pat, Rohan (7 dislikes).\n5. Lasagna: Liked by Ana, Jay, Mei, Lei, Sky (5 likes). Disliked by Li, Xiu, Chao, Sue, Ty, Wei, Anil, Lan, Pat, Ru (10 dislikes).\n6. Churros: Liked by Li, Xiu, Ned, Ty, Pat (5 likes). Disliked by Ana, Max, Lei, Rex, Ansh (5 dislikes).\n\nWith these likes and dislikes, our goal is to satisfy all individuals with at least one of their likes on the "orderable" list or with one of their dislikes on the "not_orderable" list.\n\nHere\'s how we can proceed:\n\n1. Lasagna has the most dislikes, so it\'s a candidate for "not_orderable". However, we cannot include Lasagna in "not_orderable", because Jay likes it and all his dislikes cannot be included in "orderable". Therefore, Lasagna has to be in "orderable".\n2. Since Lasagna is "orderable", Lan, Sue, Ty, Wei, Anil, Pat, Ru cannot have any of their dislikes as "orderable" so their likes must be included in "orderable".\n3. Cheese satisfies Wes, Li, Ty, Hui, Sue, and it can\'t be "not_orderable" because Sky likes it and doesn\'t have other likes to satisfy him. So, Cheese must be "orderable".\n4. Nobody that dislikes Cheesecake has only dislikes, which means we can satisfy them with their dislikes in "not_orderable". Therefore, Cheesecake can be "orderable" to satisfy its likers.\n5. With Lasagna, Cheese, and Cheesecake in "orderable", Jay, Li, Chao, Sky, Hui, Gen, Ana, Xiu, Ansh, and Sue can be satisfied with their likes. Lin and Wei are satisfied with Cheese as a dislike in "orderable".\n6. Max and Rohan are satisfied with their likes being "orderable".\n7. Ty cannot have Cheesecake as "orderable", so Churros must be "orderable". This satisfies Ty and Pat.\n8. Ned likes Lasagna and Churros which are "orderable"