ze them based on the preferences:\n\n- Soup: Liked by Lia, Kavi, Veer, Naina; Disliked by Chao, Amy.\n- Sorbet: Disliked by Lin, Lia, Kavi, Pat, Neil.\n- Paneer: Liked by Naina; Disliked by Lin, Ru, Hui.\n- Guacamole: Liked by Rex, Hui, Naina, Mel; Disliked by Lia, Neil, Gus.\n- Poke: Liked by Rex, Neil, Nic; Disliked by Lin, Chao.\n- Bread: Liked by Kavi, Amy, Ru, Mel; Disliked by Riya, Hui, May, Nic.\n- Falafel: Liked by Rex, Veer, May; Disliked by Amy, Riya, Sia, Neil.\n- Brownies: Liked by Ru, Sia, Pat, Mel; Disliked by May, Gus.\n- Salad: Liked by Riya, Gus; Disliked by Sia, Pat.\n- Guacamole, Poke, and Brownies: Liked and disliked by various people, no clear solution.\n- Bread and Falafel: A lot of conflict, can\'t be easily placed in either list.\n  \nGiven the likes and dislikes, looking for non-conflicting likes:\n- Salad is only liked by Riya and Gus and is disliked by Sia and Pat, which means it must be in neither or the \'not_orderable\' list.\n- Soup is liked by many and can\'t be in the \'not_orderable\' because it\'s liked (Amy dislikes soup but likes bread which is conflicted, Chao dislikes everything).\n- Sorbet is universally disliked, so it can go into the \'not_orderable\' list.\n\nLet\'s tentatively put "Sorbet" in the \'not_orderable\' list since every person who dislikes it, doesn\'t like it.\n\nNow let\'s check for items liked by multiple people but not afflicting with dislikes:\n- Bread is liked by Kavi, Amy, Ru, Mel; however, it is disliked by Riya, Hui, May, Nic. Since multiple people like it and multiple people dislike it, we cannot immediately make a decision. Let\'s see if it conflicts with other likes of those who dislike it:\n  - Riya likes salad (which is conflicted).\n  - Hui likes guacamole (which is conflicted).\n  - May likes falafel (which is conflicted).\n  - Nic likes poke (which is conflicted).\n  With no clear options, bread remains a contentious item.\n  \nHaving \'soup\' and \'bread\' both liked by Kavi makes one of them a