ut also disliked by even more participants, making it a candidate for 'not_orderable'.\n3. **Falafel is also controversial:** It has several likes but also many dislikes.\n4. **Tart:** Liked by some but disliked by two, no strong feeling overall.\n5. **Biscuits:** Liked by a few and disliked by a few.\n6. **Gelato and Sorbet:** Mixed feelings, liked by some, disliked by others.\n\nSo to satisfy the highest number of individuals, we will aim to put the most disliked items, especially if they are disliked by those who like fewer things, in the 'not_orderable' list, and the less disliked or liked items, especially if liked by those who dislike fewer things, in the 'orderable' list.\n\n### Potential 'not_orderable' Items:\n\n- **Shawarma:** It is disliked by many, liked by fewer, and some of them (Hal and Rob) have other likes (Hummus).\n\n### Potential 'orderable' Items:\n\n- **Hummus:** Hal likes it and doesn't dislike anything that isn't already heavy in dislikes.\n- **Tart:** Liked by Kim, Abe, and Bo, and only Sia and Jon have it in dislikes.\n\n### Building the Lists:\n\nLet's now start adding items to the lists based on these preferences, to ensure everyone's satisfaction:\n\n1. **Shawarma to 'not_orderable':** This satisfies Kim, Liz, Mina, Nita, Tia, and Jon just by this addition since they all dislike it.\n\n2. **Hummus to 'orderable':** This will satisfy Hal and it's not disliked by anyone else.\n\n3. **Tart to 'orderable':** This will satisfy Kim (who dislikes Shawarma and is already in 'not_orderable'), Abe, and Bo. Sia dislikes Tart but likes and can be satisfied by Biscuits. Jon dislikes Tart, but he likes Gelato, which has no strong opposition.\n\n### Checking Remaining Participants:\n\n- **Naina is now satisfied** because Falafel (which she likes) isn't in 'not_orderable'.\n- **Rob is now satisfied** with Shawarma in 'not_orderable'.\n- **Liz is satisfied** because Shawarma is in 'not_orderable'.\n- **Dan is satisfied** since Falafel (which he dislikes)