al individuals and disliked by several, so it should also not be in either list.\n- `roti`, `fries`, `gelato`, `nachos`, `churros` all have conflicts in liking and disliking, so they should also not be in either list.\n\nBy ensuring that `hummus` is in `not_orderable` and `kebab` and `omelette` are in `orderable`, all participants are indirectly satisfied according to the rules:\n- Those who like `hummus` can be satisfied because their dislike in `not_orderable` satisfies them.\n- Those who like `kebab` and `omelette` are directly satisfied.\n\nWe can thus confidently conclude our lists are:\n\n```python\norderable=['kebab', 'omelette'], not_orderable=['hummus']\n```\n\nIt should be noted that this solution is one of the potentially many that exist, as the problem could have multiple valid arrangements that satisfy all individuals.", 'num_prompt_tokens': 467, 'num_completion_tokens': 934}
