e' list.\n- Sushi is liked by Cal, Wei, Lei, Bo, and disliked by Diya, Anil, Jim, Oli, Ben, Val, May, Om; because it's disliked by more people than liked, we should consider it for the 'not_orderable' list as well.\n- Ravioli is liked by Rina, Anil, Lei, Geet, Mei, Sam, and disliked by Sid, May, Val, Tom; more people like ravioli compared to those who dislike it, so we could consider it for 'orderable'.\n- Cheese is liked by Sid, Gen, Oli, Sia, and disliked by Jim, Lei, Geet, Wei; because it's liked and disliked almost equally, it's a tricky choice, but initially, let's not place it on any list.\n- Shrimps are liked by Cal, Rina, Val, and disliked by Jim, Wei, Oli, Gen, May; seeing a similar pattern as lobster and sushi, we might put shrimps on the 'not_orderable' list.\n- Hummus is liked by Diya, Sid, Geet, Ben, and disliked by Pat, Tom, Sam; given its popularity, we should consider hummus for the 'orderable' list.\n- Naan is liked by Cal, Pat, Sam, Sia, Ben, Om and disliked by Anil; its popularity suggests it should be 'orderable'.\n\nWorking through the list while remembering to satisfy everyone, we find:\n\n1. Hummus is liked by several people and only disliked by a few, so we place hummus on the 'orderable' list.\n2. Both lobster and shrimps are disliked by multiple people and liked by fewer, so we will put lobster and shrimps on the 'not_orderable' list.\n3. Sushi has many detractors compared to supporters, so we place it in the 'not_orderable' list as well.\n4. Ravioli is liked by many but disliked by a critical few (in fact by May who dislikes everything else), this must then go into the 'orderable' list to satisfy them.\n5. Cheese is tricky due to its divisive nature, but because sushi, lobster, and shrimp are on the 'not_orderable' list, it can remain off both lists for now as the people who like it will be satisfied by other items on the 'orderable' list.\n6. Naan is widely liked and can go on the 'orderable' list to satisfy those who like it.\n\nNow we need to check if everyone is satisfied:\n\n- Diya will be satisfied with hummus being orderable.\n- Sid will be satisfied with hummus being orderable.\n- Rina will be satisfied with shrimps being not orderable or ravioli being orderable.\n- Cal will be satisfied because naan is orderable despite sushi being not orderable.\n- Anil will be satisfied with ravioli being orderable despite sushi being not orderable.\n- Jim will be satisfied with sushi and shrimps being not orderable.\n- Lei will be satisfied with sushi being not orderable.\n- Geet will be satisfied with hummus and ravioli being orderable.\n- Wei will be satisfied with sushi and shrimps being not orderable.\n- Pat will be satisfied with naan being orderable despite lobster not being orderable.\n- Gen will be satisfied with lobster and shrimps being not orderable.\n- Mei will be satisfied with ravioli being orderable despite lobster not being orderable.\n- Oli will be satisfied with sushi and shrimps being not orderable.\n- May will be satisfied with sushi, shrimps, and ravioli in respective lists.\n- Val will be satisfied with shrimps being not orderable.\n- Sam will be satisfied with ravioli and naan being orderable despite hummus being orderable.\n- Bo will be satisfied with lobster being not orderable.\n- Sia will be satisfied with naan being orderable.\n- Ben will be satisfied with naan and hummus being orderable.\n- Om will be satisfied with naan being orderable and sushi being not orderable.\n- Tom will be satisfied with lobster and hummus being on the respective lists.\n\nSince no conflicts emerge and all participants are satisfied, we can now write the final solution:\n\n```python\norderable=['hummus', 'ravioli', 'naan'], not_orderable=['lobster', 'sushi', 'shrimps']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 474, 'num_completion_tokens': 1089}
