t since there's nothing they both like that is disliked by anyone else, we must satisfy them on the dislikes side:\n\n  For Arun, who dislikes poke and likes tiramisu, we have to avoid poke and tiramisu on 'orderable' to satisfy him (as long as poke gets on 'not_orderable').\n  For Eva, who dislikes poke, we have to ensure poke is on 'not_orderable' because all her likes are disliked by someone else.\n\n- 'Poke' being on 'not_orderable' satisfies Abe, Ru, Sid, Eva, and Wes on their dislikes.\n\nNow we have burger on 'orderable' and poke on 'not_orderable'. Let's see if this satisfies everyone:\n\n- Ping is satisfied with burger.\n- Bao gets burger.\n- Neil can't get caramel, but since we can't satisfy him with the likes, we need to satisfy him with a dislike.\n  - Omelette is liked by many so we can't use that.\n  - Tiramisu is liked by many, so we can't use that either.\n  - We can't satisfy Neil's criteria with the current selections.\n- Ray is satisfied because poke is 'not_orderable'.\n- Tara is satisfied with burger.\n- Mei can't get their like caramel, so we need a dislike:\n  - Can't use omelette since it is liked by others.\n  - Tiramisu is liked by many, so can't use it.\n  - We can't satisfy Mei's criteria with the current selections.\n- Abe is satisfied because poke is 'not_orderable'.\n- Arun is satisfied with the dislikes met.\n- Ru is satisfied because poke is 'not_orderable'.\n- Geet is satisfied with burger.\n- Mel gets burger.\n- Isha is satisfied with burger.\n- Sid is satisfied because poke is 'not_orderable'.\n- Wes is satisfied because poke is 'not_orderable'.\n- Jay gets burger.\n- Eva is satisfied because poke is 'not_orderable'.\n- Meg is satisfied with burger.\n- Gen is satisfied with burger.\n\nBased on this, the current selection doesn't work because we can't satisfy Neil and Mei with the current selections. To solve the issue for Neil and Mei, we can look at their options:\n\n- Neil dislikes omelette and tiramisu but likes caramel. However, caramel is disliked by others.\n- Mei dislikes caramel, omelette, and tiramisu but doesn't have a like we can use to satisfy.\n\nIf we place caramel on 'orderable', we can satisfy Neil, but Ping and Jay dislike it; we would need to satisfy Ping and Jay using dislikes:\n\n- Jay can be satisfied by placing caramel on 'orderable'.\n- Ping, however, dislikes caramel and getting another item from their likes (nachos or burger) would conflict with others' dislikes too.\n\nSince many people like and dislike the same items, we can't satisfy one person without disappointing another. Due to the overlapping likes and dislikes, any combination we try leads to a conflict, and it's not possible to satisfy all participants.\n\nTherefore, the solution is to output empty lists for both 'orderable' and 'not_orderable':\n\n```python\norderable = []\nnot_orderable = []\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 437, 'num_completion_tokens': 1387}
