be "orderable". However, we find an issue because both Eva and Lin like pizza and dislike all other mentioned items, so pizza must be in the "orderable" list to satisfy them. But this conflicts with Ray, Jan, May, and Pam who dislike pizza and no other item among their dislikes can be in the "not_orderable" list to satisfy them. Due to this mutually exclusive constraint, we conclude that it is not possible to satisfy all members of the group.\n\nHence, we arrive at empty lists for both "orderable" and "not_orderable".\n\nThe final Python code output that shows the empty lists would be:\n```python\norderable = [], not_orderable = []\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 1530, 'num_completion_tokens': 556}
