"orderable".\n\nStep 5: With burger in "not_orderable" and ramen in "orderable", let\'s check if all participants are satisfied. All except Sol, Qi, Cal, Ping, Ava, Ansh, Yan, Tim, and Ned like either ramen or dislike burger. However, we\'ve put naan (liked by Sol, Cal, Yan, Ansh, and Tim) in neither list yet.\n\nStep 6: To satisfy the remaining participants, we need to include naan in "orderable" or churros in "orderable" for Cal and Raj. Naan can be put in "orderable" since Qi\'s and Cal\'s satisfaction come from having burger in "not_orderable" and they do not have any other item in their dislike list that is not already covered.\n\nWe now have a potential solution with burger in "not_orderable", and both ramen and naan in "orderable". To verify:\n\n- Everyone who likes burger has another liked item in "orderable" or dislikes something in "not_orderable".\n- Everyone who dislikes burger but likes ramen or naan is satisfied by their inclusion in "orderable".\n\nTherefore, the solution is:\n```\norderable=[\'ramen\', \'naan\'], not_orderable=[\'burger\']\n```', 'num_prompt_tokens': 619, 'num_completion_tokens': 874}
