rderable.'\n\nLet's examine the information given:\n\n### Dislikes salad, poke, burger:\n- Ben\n- Ken\n- Isha\n- Anil\n- Ana\n- Eli\n- Kavi\n  \nThese individuals dislike all offered dishes, they cannot help us to determine which dishes belong to the 'orderable' list since they dislike everything. They cannot contribute to satisfying the conditions, and hence will be neutral in decision-making.\n\n### Likes at least one thing:\nOthers all like at least one thing. If we can find a common item that satisfies all individuals who like something, we can place it on the 'orderable' list.\n\nLet's find commonalities in likes:\n- Poke is liked by: Ian, Rob, Yue, Lou, Cy, Dan, Naina, Qi, Ping\n- Burger is liked by: Rob, Val, Xiu, Raj, Ravi, Sol, Mia, Tim, Taj\n- Salad is liked by: Jay, Val, Dan, Zac, Wes, Mia, Min, Ping, Taj\n\nNow let's find conflicts, i.e., where an item liked by one is disliked by another:\n- Poke is disliked by: Jay, Val, Zac, Min, Wes, Salad, Isha, Ana, Kavi\n- Burger is disliked by: Ian, Yue, Lou, Dan, Naina, Qi, Ping, Isha, Ana, Kavi\n- Salad is disliked by: Ian, Rob, Cy, Raj, Ravi, Qi, Ping, Isha, Ana, Kavi\n\nGiven these conflicts, we cannot satisfy everyone using only one item on the 'orderable' list as some people's likes are others' dislikes. Since no single item stands out as universally liked, we see that 'poke', 'burger', and 'salad' all have conflicts, i.e., each is liked by some but disliked by others. Thus, satisfying everyone is not possible using the criteria provided.\n\nEvery item is liked by someone and disliked by someone else. There is no single item that can be placed on the 'orderable' list without leaving at least one person unsatisfied due to their dislikes. Similarly, there is no item that can be placed on the 'not_orderable' list without leaving at least one person unsatisfied due to their likes. Therefore, the lists must be:\n\n```\norderable = []\nnot_orderable = []\n```\n\nThese empty lists indicate that no combination of 'orderable' and 'not_orderable' will satisfy the entire group's preferences based on the given constraints.", 'num_prompt_tokens': 515, 'num_completion_tokens': 590}
