 'not_orderable' list.\n- Everyone who likes korma is satisfied because it is on the 'orderable' list.\n- Everyone who likes salad is also satisfied.\n\nIt appears that we have a solution that satisfies all the criteria. However, this is a complex problem with many individuals and preferences, so it's possible that manual verification might miss conflicts. In a real situation, this configuration should be validated with an algorithm to make sure that all individuals are indeed satisfied.\n\nHere is the output:\n\n```python\norderable = ['salad', 'korma'], not_orderable = ['cake']\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 1561, 'num_completion_tokens': 1068}
