ng techniques or algorithms designed for this purpose.\n\nIt is clear, though, that this problem might not have a unique solution, and is potentially unsolvable by manual means due to the complexity. It is implied that a computer algorithm that can handle constraint satisfaction problems should be used to find a solution which satisfies all the given constraints or to determine that no such solution exists. \n\nUnfortunately, without such a computational method, I cannot provide you with the exact \'orderable\' and \'not_orderable\' lists here. If you had access to a computer and could code, you might use a constraint solver or write a backtracking algorithm to find the solution.', 'num_prompt_tokens': 1115, 'num_completion_tokens': 520}
