isfy Xiu, Lou, Bea, Meg, Tim, Kim, Lex, Shan, Zac, Mel, Ravi, Ned (likes macaron), Wei (likes macaron), Jay (likes macaron), Pat (dislikes ramen, burger), Eva, Raj (likes macaron), Sam (dislikes macaron), and Oli (dislikes macaron).\n- They also don't share a common dislike.\n\nTrying Custard or Burger as 'orderable' will lead to similar conflicts.\n\nAfter examining all the possibilities, we find that no single item or combination of items can be placed in 'orderable' without some participants being dissatisfied, while compensating with the 'not_orderable' list is not possible since the dissatisfied participants do not share a common dislike.\n\nTherefore, it appears that there is no possible combination of 'orderable' and 'not_orderable' that satisfies all participants. Hence, both lists should be empty.\n\nFinal solution:\n\n```python\norderable = []\nnot_orderable = []\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 884, 'num_completion_tokens': 866}
