ine without). Assign: Orderable.\n- Shawarma is liked by a good number of persons and the persons who dislike it are not very strongly against it. Assign: Orderable.\n- Quiche is more disliked than liked, and those who like quiche also like other foods that could be orderable. Assign: Not orderable.\n\nAfter the initial assignments:\norderable = ['tart', 'shawarma']\nnot_orderable = ['quiche']\n\nNow, let's see if everyone is satisfied:\n\n- Rex likes tart (satisfied).\n- Anil dislikes quiche (satisfied).\n- Tim dislikes quiche (satisfied).\n- Eli likes tart (satisfied).\n- Jan dislikes quiche (satisfied).\n- Zoe will be unsatisfied because quiche was not ordered but her liked foods are not yet ordered. We need to add spaghetti for her, but doing so will unsatisfy Eli, Ian, Ray, and Cy (not satisfying since many people dislike it).\n- Zac likes biscuits, but since more people dislike them, we're not adding them yet, thus he is currently unsatisfied.\n- Ty likes shawarma (satisfied).\n- Shan has shawarma and dislikes biscuits, thus satisfied with current assignments.\n- Ian likes shawarma and biscuits, but biscuits aren't a deal-breaker yet. He's satisfied.\n- Lin likes tart (satisfied).\n- Rohan likes tart and shawarma, even though he dislikes the latter, he is satisfied because tart is on the list.\n- Ray dislikes quiche (satisfied).\n- Ying likes pancakes, which we have not added as dislike for them is dominant (she's unsatisfied).\n- Ula likes tart (satisfied).\n- Wes likes tart (satisfied).\n- Eva likes shawarma (satisfied).\n- Cy likes shawarma (satisfied).\n- Jaya likes tart (satisfied).\n- Lex dislikes quiche (satisfied).\n- Chao likes shawarma (satisfied).\n\nSo Zoe, Zac, Ying, and those who like spaghetti are not satisfied.\n\nTo satisfy Zoe and avoid spaghetti, we can add anything else Zoe likes or dislikes that's not on the list yet. However, Zoe also likes pancake and dislikes tart, and both options are conflicting. At this point, it's clear that there i