aloo, biscuits\n\nFrom the list, we can see that:\n- "doughnut" and "shawarma" are disliked by several people, so they cannot be in the \'orderable\' list if we want to satisfy everyone.\n- "biscuits" are liked by many and only one person dislikes them. \n- "vindaloo" is liked by many and only two people dislike it.\n- "brownies" are less controversial, with only one person disliking them.\n\nStep 1:\n- Place "doughnut" and "shawarma" in the \'not_orderable\' list as they are strongly disliked.\n- Since Sol dislikes "vindaloo", Kit dislikes "shawarma", Raj dislikes "doughnut", they will be satisfied by these two items not being ordered.\n- Lex and Ken, who dislike "biscuits", will also be satisfied as long as "doughnut" is not orderable.\n\nStep 2: \n- Choosing "biscuits" for the \'orderable\' list will satisfy Cy, Ana, Kit, Raj, Sol, Sal, and most likely more, but will dissatisfy Lex.\n- Instead, we can choose "vindaloo" for the \'orderable\' list as many people like it and only Sol and Jun dislike it.\n\nStep 3:\nSince we already placed "doughnut" and "shawarma" in the \'not_orderable\' list to satisfy several individuals, we can choose "vindaloo" and "brownies" for the \'orderable\' list because they are liked by multiple people except for Jun and Oli (who dislike "vindaloo") and Zoe and Oli (who dislike "brownies"). However, they will be satisfied with "shawarma" and "doughnut" in the \'not_orderable\' list, respectively.\n\nStep 4: \n- Placing "vindaloo" in the \'orderable\' list satisfies Raj, Kavi, Sam, Ty, Ansh, Oli (due to "shawarma" being in \'not_orderable\'), and Ken. \n- "brownies" will satisfy Zoe, Ansh, and Lex.\n\nFinal Step:\nWe determined that \'orderable\' can include "vindaloo" and "brownies", and \'not_orderable\' can include "doughnut" and "shawarma". Checking the remaining preferences:\n\n- Cy: Satisfied by "shawarma" being \'not_orderable\'.\n- Ana: Satisfied by "vindaloo" on \'orderable\'.\n- Kit: Satisfied by "shawarma" and "doughnut" in \'