s, so we cannot satisfy Ava no matter what we put in 'orderable'.\n- Lan dislikes biscuits, nachos, and kebab, so we also cannot satisfy Lan.\n- Zoe dislikes kebab, nachos, and biscuits, meaning we can't satisfy Zoe either.\n\nIt is impossible to satisfy Ava, Lan, and Zoe, because their dislikes cover all available foods, and they do not like anything that we can put in the 'orderable' list. Since we must satisfy all participants and we've found some that we cannot satisfy regardless of the combination, our final solution is empty lists for both 'orderable' and 'not_orderable':\n\n```python\norderable = [], not_orderable = []\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 633, 'num_completion_tokens': 534}
