ikes salmon. Dislikes ratatouille, ramen. Nic: Likes custard. Dislikes ratatouille, wonton. Mel: Likes ramen, tandoori, ratatouille. Gen: Likes burrito. Dislikes ramen, salmon. Pia: Likes tandoori, salmon. Dislikes ramen. Ru: Likes burrito, tandoori. Dislikes ramen. Om: Likes ratatouille, ramen. Dislikes burrito. Lia: Likes ramen, salmon, ratatouille. Sky: Dislikes wonton, ramen, custard. Ken: Likes wonton, custard. Dislikes tandoori. Raj: Likes tandoori, ratatouille, salmon. Ansh: Likes burrito, tandoori. Dislikes ramen. Liz: Likes ramen, salmon. Dislikes wonton. Sue: Dislikes ratatouille, wonton, burrito. Xiu: Likes burrito, custard. Dislikes ramen. Tara: Likes burrito, salmon, tandoori. Max: Likes tandoori, burrito, ratatouille. Cal: Likes burrito, salmon. Dislikes ramen. Jaya: Likes ramen, burrito, custard. Chao: Likes custard, salmon. Dislikes burrito. Veer: Likes tandoori, custard, wonton. Arun: Dislikes custard, salmon, ramen. Diya: Likes tandoori, burrito. Dislikes wonton. Rohan: Likes burrito, ratatouille. Dislikes ramen. Kim: Likes ramen, tandoori. Dislikes ratatouille. Ron: Dislikes wonton, burrito, custard. Tia: Likes burrito. Dislikes ratatouille, tandoori. Zac: Likes custard, ramen. Dislikes wonton. Neil: Likes custard, wonton. Dislikes ramen. Ty: Likes ramen, burrito. Dislikes salmon. Aarav: Likes salmon. Dislikes custard, burrito. Jun: Likes ratatouille, wonton. Dislikes custard. Vic: Likes custard, tandoori, salmon. Amy: Dislikes wonton, ramen, ratatouille. Oli: Likes wonton, salmon. Dislikes burrito. Rob: Likes custard. Dislikes tandoori, burrito. Du: Likes wonton, tandoori. Dislikes ratatouille. Anil: Likes wonton, ratatouille, ramen. Sia: Likes salmon, ratatouille. Dislikes ramen. ', 'menu_items': ['custard', 'ramen', 'salmon', 'tandoori', 'burrito', 'ratatouille', 'wonton'], 'gpt_out': "To create the two distinct lists (‘orderable’ and ‘not_orderable’), we’ll need to examine the likes and dislikes of each person carefully. We’ll start by counting the number of people who like and dislike each food item. Food items with only dislikes should go on the 'not_orderable' list, while those with only likes (and can satisfy at least one person’s dislike from the other list) should go on the 'orderable' list. Foods that are both liked and disliked present a challenge and require a more nuanced approach. Let’s start the process.\n\nCount the number of likes and dislikes for each food item:\n\nLikes:\n- Salmon: 13\n- Custard: 12\n- Ratatouille: 15\n- Burrito: 14\n- Ramen: 12\n- Tandoori: 14\n- Wonton: 7\n\nDislikes:\n- Ramen: 18\n- Salmon: 4\n- Ratatouille: 16\n- Wonton: 13\n- Custard: 7\n- Tandoori: 6\n- Burrito: 8\n\nNow, we'll look for items that only appear in the likes or only in the dislikes.\n\nItems with only dislikes (these can go to 'not_orderable'): Ramen\nItems with only likes (and can satisfy a dislike from the 'not_orderable' list if placed in 'orderable'): None\n\nNext, we deal with the items that are both liked and disliked, trying to navigate through a solution that will satisfy everyone’s preferences, which might not be possible.\n\nTo simplify, we should prioritize foods liked by more people. Ratatouille is the most liked food (15 likes), but it is also highly disliked (16), and many of the individuals who dislike ramen like ratatouille, so it cannot be on the 'not_orderable' list.\n\nLet's place ratatouille in 'orderable' and ensure any person disliking ratatouille has something in 'not_orderable'. Checking the list:\n- Anyone disliking ratatouille also dislikes ramen, except Liv, who dislikes burrito and tandoori in addition to ratatouille. Since ratatouille needs to be 'orderable' to satisfy the majority, Liv cannot be satisfied.\n\nUnfortunately, because we cannot satisfy Liv's condition while also needing to satisfy the majority for ratatouille, no combination exists that satisfies all participants. Considering this, our final solution must be empty lists for both 'orderable' and 'not_orderable':\n\n```python\norderable = []\nnot_orderable = []\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 1126, 'num_completion_tokens': 552}
