ble', and check:\n\n- Everyone who likes sushi (which is quite a number of people) will find at least one item they like in the 'orderable' list.\n- Everyone who likes pizza will also find at least one item they like in the 'orderable' list.\n- Everyone who dislikes burrito will find it in the 'not_orderable' list.\n\nSince this satisfies all criteria for everyone except Sia and Shan, the final solution would be:\n\n```python\norderable = ['sushi', 'pizza']\nnot_orderable = ['burrito']\n```\n\nHowever, since we cannot ignore Sia and Shan, and it is impossible to satisfy them due to their complete dislike of all items, the only valid outcome while including them is:\n\n```python\norderable = []\nnot_orderable = []\n```", 'num_prompt_tokens': 478, 'num_completion_tokens': 729}
