nd liked by none, we can safely add it to 'not_orderable'. We cannot do the same with tart immediately as it's liked by Mel, so we will consider it later if required.\n\nNow, let’s go through each person's likes and try to fill the 'orderable' list:\n\n1. If we include udon, we satisfy Eli, Jim, Aarav, Lin, Lei, and Jaya (6 people). But this will dissatisfy Wes, Mel, and Sam since they dislike udon.\n2. Including tandoori satisfies Tom, Zan, Lei, and Wes (4 people), with no direct conflicts.\n3. Including salmon satisfies Zan, Lia, Meg, Pat (4 people), but is disliked by Tom, Jun, Lou, Aarav, Kim, Lin, Max (7 people).\n4. Including nachos satisfies Eli, Lou, Meg, Pat (4 people), but is disliked by Aarav, Zan, Lia, and Max (4 people).\n5. Including brownies satisfies Jun, Kim, Sam, Veer, Ty, Max, Pat (7 people), but is disliked by Tom and Mel (2 people).\n\nBased on this analysis, brownies should definitely be on the 'orderable' list as it satisfies the most people with the least conflict.\n\nBefore finalizing the lists, let's count how many people would be satisfied by our current choice:\n\n- Brownies are on 'orderable', satisfying Jun, Kim, Sam, Veer, Ty, Max, and Pat.\n- Caramel is on 'not_orderable', satisfying Lou, Aarav, Sam, Veer, Lia, Max, and Lei by their dislike of caramel.\n\nWe need to be careful about the remaining choices, as they can cause conflicts. We avoid udon and nachos for now because they are both liked and disliked by several people.\n\nTo satisfy the most remaining people without conflicting with our 'orderable' brownies:\n\n- Tandoori (satisfying 4 more people – Tom, Zan, Lei, Wes) is a better choice than salmon, as salmon has too many dislikes.\n\nNow let's check who is left unsatisfied:\n\n- Eli: needs nachos or udon\n- Jim: needs waffles or udon\n- Jun: is satisfied (brownies on 'orderable')\n- Lou: is satisfied (caramel on 'not_orderable')\n- Aarav: satisfied (caramel on 'not_orderable')\n- Wes: satisfied (tandoori on 'orderable')\n- Zan